hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna Abu Muhammad informed us, saying: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, from Ali ibn Rabi'a al-Walibi, from Asma ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, who said: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah Almighty benefited me with whatever He willed of it, and when anyone else narrated to me I made him swear an oath, and when he swore to me I believed him. Then Abu Bakr narrated to me - and Abu Bakr spoke the truth - saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no servant who commits a sin, then stands and performs ablution and performs it well, then prays two rak'ahs, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that Allah forgives him. Sufyan said: And Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likewise, adding therein: except that he said: and he shows devotion, meaning he prays."
"2","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid ibn Muslim al-Dimashqi narrated to us: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir saying: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir saying: I heard Awsat al-Bajali, while upon the minbar of Hims, saying: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq saying, while upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then tears choked him, then he returned and tears choked him, then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying in the previous year: Ask Allah for pardon and well-being, for no servant has been given anything after certainty better than well-being."
"3","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim: that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, you recite this verse: O you who believe, take care of yourselves; he who goes astray cannot harm you when you are guided. And we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When people see the wrongdoer and do not seize his hand, Allah is about to envelop them all in punishment."
"4","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us: Mis'ar ibn Kidam and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira al-Thaqafi, from Ali ibn Rabi'a al-Walibi, from Asma ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed of it, and when anyone else narrated to me I made him swear, and when he swore to me I believed him, and Abu Bakr narrated to me - and Abu Bakr spoke the truth - saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who commits a sin and performs ablution and performs it well. Mis'ar said: then he prays. And Sufyan said: then he prays two rak'ahs and seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that he is forgiven."
"5","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sa'd ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us: my brother Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from his grandfather Abu Sa'id al-Maqburi, that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib saying: No narrator narrated to me a hadith I had not myself heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that I commanded him to swear by Allah that he heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - except Abu Bakr, for he never lied. Then Abu Bakr narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant mentions a sin he committed, then stands when he remembers that sin, performs ablution and performs it well, then prays two rak'ahs, then seeks Allah's forgiveness for that sin, except that He forgives him."
"6","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Barza, who said: I passed by Abu Bakr al-Siddiq while he was enraged at one of his companions, and I said: O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, who is this you are enraged at? He said: Why do you ask about him? I said: I will strike his neck. He said: By Allah, what I said dispelled his anger. Then he said: That was for no one after Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad al-Rassasi narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us: Yazid ibn Khumayr informed me, saying: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir - a man of Himyar - narrating from Awsat ibn Isma'il ibn Awsat al-Bajali, from Abu Bakr, that he heard him, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the previous year in this place of mine, then he wept and said: Hold to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and both are in Paradise; and beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and both are in the Fire; and ask Allah for well-being, for no servant has been given after certainty anything better than well-being. He said: And do not sever ties, nor turn your backs on one another, nor hate one another, nor envy one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"8","The narrations of Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us: I heard Abu Ubayd saying: I attended the Eid with Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he began with the prayer before the sermon and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting these two days: the day of Fitr and the day of Adha. As for the day of Fitr, it is the day of your breaking fast from your fasting, and as for the day of Adha, eat therein from the meat of your sacrifices. Then I attended the Eid with Uthman ibn Affan, and it coincided with Friday, and he began with the prayer before the sermon, then said: This is a day in which two Eids have gathered for the Muslims, so whoever is here from the people of al-Awali and wishes to leave, we have permitted him, and whoever wishes to remain, let him remain. Then I attended the Eid with Ali ibn Abi Talib, and he began with the prayer before the sermon and said: Let no one eat of the meat of his sacrifice beyond three days. Abu Bakr al-Humaydi said: I said to Sufyan: They raise this last statement from Ali ibn Abi Talib. Sufyan said: I do not preserve it as raised to the Prophet, and it is abrogated."
"9","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us: I heard Abdullah ibn Sarjis saying: I saw the bald Umar ibn al-Khattab come to the Black Stone and kiss it, then say: By Allah, I know that you are a stone that neither harms nor benefits, and had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would not have kissed you."
"10","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Subayh al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ma'dan ibn Abi Talha al-Ya'mari, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he said: I consider that you eat two trees - meaning two foul ones - onions and garlic; if you must do so, kill them by cooking, then eat them, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he found their smell on a man, order him to be taken out to al-Baqi'."
"11","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrating from Umar ibn al-Khattab the like of it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that Husayn did not mention Ma'dan."
"12","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, first before we met al-Zuhri, from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, who said: I came with a hundred dinars seeking exchange, and Talha said: We have exchange; wait until our treasurer comes from al-Ghaba. And he took the hundred dinars from me. Then Umar said to me: Do not leave him, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for silver is usury except hand to hand, wheat for wheat is usury except hand to hand, barley for barley is usury except hand to hand, and dates for dates is usury except hand to hand. Then when al-Zuhri came he did not mention this introductory account. And I heard al-Zuhri saying: I heard Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan al-Nasri saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for silver is usury except hand to hand, wheat for wheat is usury except hand to hand, barley for barley is usury except hand to hand, and dates for dates is usury except hand to hand. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: And this is the most authentic hadith reported from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on this subject, meaning on exchange."
"13","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Tawus informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: It reached Umar ibn al-Khattab that Samura sold wine, so he said: May Allah destroy Samura; did he not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they melted them and sold them, meaning they dissolved them."
"14","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, saying: So-and-so informed me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab upon the minbar saying - with his hand upon the minbar thus, meaning moving it right and left: A petty worker of ours in Iraq, a petty worker of ours in Iraq, mixed into the fay' of the Muslims the prices of wine and pigs, though the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah cursed the Jews; fats were forbidden to them, so they melted them and sold them, meaning they dissolved them."
"15","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard Malik ibn Anas asking Zayd ibn Aslam, and Zayd said: I heard my father saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: I gave a horse in the path of Allah, then I saw it being sold, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I buy it? He said: Do not buy it, and do not go back on your charity."
"16","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ibn Sirin, from Umar ibn al-Khattab similarly, except that he said: he saw it being sold, or some of its offspring."
"17","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Ubaydillah al-Umari narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'a, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umra, for following up between them increases the lifespan and removes poverty and sins, just as the bellows removes dross. Sufyan said: Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated this hadith to us from Abda, from Asim; then when Abda arrived we went to him to ask him about it, and he said: Asim only narrated it to me, and here is Asim present; so we went to Asim and asked him about it, and he narrated it to us thus. Then I heard it from him after that; sometimes he stopped it upon Umar without mentioning his father therein, but most of the time he narrated it from Abdullah ibn Amir, from his father, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sufyan said: And sometimes we were silent about this phrase, increases the lifespan, and did not narrate it, fearing these - meaning the Qadariyya - would argue with it, though they have no proof in it."
"18","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Abda ibn Abi Lubaba narrated to us - we memorized it from him more than once - saying: I heard Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salama saying, often saying: Masruq and I went to al-Subayy ibn Ma'bad to recall this hadith with him, and al-Subayy said: I was a Christian man, then I became Muslim and set out intending Hajj; when I was at al-Qadisiyya I entered ihram for Hajj and Umra together, and Salman ibn Rabi'a and Zayd ibn Suhan heard me and said: This one is more astray than his family's camel. It was as though a mountain was laid upon me by their two words. Then I met Umar ibn al-Khattab and informed him, and he turned to them and blamed them, then turned to me and said: You have been guided to the Sunna of your Prophet; you have been guided to the Sunna of your Prophet. Sufyan said: meaning that he had joined Hajj and Umra with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he permitted it, not that he himself did it."
"19","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn Muslim and Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, saying: al-Awza'i narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, saying: Ikrima, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying while in Wadi al-Aqiq: Tonight a comer from my Lord came to me and said: Pray in this blessed valley and say: An Umra within a Hajj."
"20","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, saying: My father informed me, saying: I heard Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab narrating from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the night approaches from here, and the day departs from here, and the sun has set, the fasting person has broken his fast."
"21","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ma'mar and others, from al-Zuhri, from al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid, from Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza, from Ibn al-Sa'di: that he came to Umar ibn al-Khattab from Syria, and Umar said to him: Have I not been told that you administer some of the works of the Muslims and are given your wage but do not accept it? I said: Yes; I have horses and slaves, and I am well-off, and I want my work to be charity for the Muslims. So Umar said: Do not do that, for I intended the same as you intended, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give me gifts, and I would say: Give it to one needier than I; and once he gave me wealth, and I said: Give it to one needier than I. So he said: O Umar, whatever Allah brings you of this wealth without asking and without the soul aspiring to it, take it, acquire wealth with it and give charity from it; and whatever is otherwise, do not set your soul after it."
"22","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar and Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that he heard Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was of what Allah granted His Messenger as fay', over which the Muslims did not urge horses or camels, so it belonged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) exclusively; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would spend from it upon his family a year's maintenance, and what remained he put into horses and weapons as preparation in the path of Allah. Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan only said in this hadith: he would withhold from it a year's maintenance."
"23","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Ajfa al-Sulami, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: Beware, do not inflate the dowries of women, for had it been an honor in this world or piety with Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have been the most deserving of it among you; I do not know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to have married any of his wives or wedded any of his daughters for more than twelve uqiyyas; yet today one of you inflates the woman's dowry until it becomes enmity in his own soul, and he says: I was burdened for you with the carrying-strap of the waterskin. He said: I was a young lad and did not know what the carrying-strap of the waterskin was. He said: And another thing you say of some who are killed in these campaigns of yours: So-and-so was killed a martyr, or so-and-so died a martyr, though perhaps he had loaded the sides of his mount or its rear with gold or silver, seeking trade; so do not say that, but say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - or as Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah is in Paradise. Sufyan said: Ayyub would always doubt it thus, and Sufyan said: If Hammad ibn Zayd narrated it thus, well and good, otherwise it was not preserved."
"24","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, saying: My father informed me, saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab sent for an old man of Banu Zuhra from our neighborhood who had reached the pre-Islamic age, and I came with the old man to Umar while he was in al-Hijr; Umar asked him about children of the pre-Islamic age, and the old man said: As for the sperm, it is from so-and-so, and as for the child, it is upon the bed of so-and-so. So Umar said: You have spoken truly, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by the bed. Then when the old man left, Umar called him and said: Inform me about the building of the Ka'ba. He said: Quraysh gathered strength to build the Ka'ba but fell short and proved too weak, so they left part of it in al-Hijr. So Umar said: You have spoken truly."
"25","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab upon the minbar saying: Allah sent Muhammad with the truth and revealed the Book to him, and among what was revealed to him was the verse of stoning; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, and we stoned after him. Sufyan said: I heard it from al-Zuhri at length and memorized some things from it, and this is of what I did not memorize from it that day."
"26","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: We came to al-Zuhri in the house of Ibn al-Jawwaz, and he said: If you wish I will narrate to you twenty hadiths, and if you wish I will narrate to you the hadith of al-Saqifa; and I was the youngest of the people, and I wished he would not narrate it due to its length; but the people said: Narrate to us the hadith of al-Saqifa. So al-Zuhri narrated it to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba ibn Mas'ud, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, and I memorized some things from it; then Ma'mar narrated the remainder of it to me afterwards."
"27","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab upon the minbar saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not extol me as the Christians extolled the son of Maryam; I am only His servant, so say: His servant and His Messenger."
"28","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi informed me that he heard Alqama ibn Waqqas al-Laythi saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab upon the minbar reporting that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Actions are only by intentions, and every man has only what he intended; so whoever's emigration was to Allah and His Messenger, his emigration is to Allah and His Messenger, and whoever's emigration was to a worldly gain he attains or a woman he marries, his emigration is to that to which he emigrated."
"29","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Yahya ibn Subayh al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ma'dan ibn Abi Talha al-Ya'mari, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he said upon the minbar: I saw in a dream as though a rooster pecked me three times, or pecked me with three pecks; and I said: a non-Arab; and I have assigned this matter after me to these six with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while pleased with them: Uthman, Ali, al-Zubayr, Talha, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas; so whomever is appointed caliph, he is the caliph."
"30","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, saying: My father informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: When Umar ibn al-Khattab prayed a prayer he would sit for the people; whoever had a need would speak to him, and if no one had a need he would stand and enter. Then he prayed some prayers in which he did not sit for the people. Ibn Abbas said: So I attended at the door and said: O Yarfa, is the Commander of the Believers ill? He said: The Commander of the Believers has no complaint. So I sat, then Uthman ibn Affan came and sat; then Yarfa came out and said: Stand, O Ibn Affan; stand, O Ibn Abbas. So we entered upon Umar, and before him were heaps of wealth, upon each heap a covering; and Umar said: I looked among the people of Madina and found you two of the largest in clan, so take this wealth and divide it, and whatever is surplus, return it. As for Uthman, he scooped up, and as for me, I knelt upon my knees and said: And if there is a shortfall, will you make it up to us? So Umar said: A pebble from a rugged mountain - meaning a stone from a mountain - was this not with Allah when Muhammad and his companions ate dried meat? I said: Yes indeed, by Allah, this was with Allah while Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive, and had it been opened to him he would have done with it other than what you do. He said: So Umar became angry and said: Then what would he have done? I said: Then he would have eaten and fed us. He said: So Umar sobbed until his ribs shook, then said: I wish I could leave it even, neither for me nor against me."
"31","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar and others, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: A Jewish man said to Umar ibn al-Khattab: Had this verse been revealed upon us, This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed upon you My favor and approved for you Islam as religion, we would have taken that day as a festival. So Umar said: I know on which day this verse was revealed; it was revealed on the day of Arafa, on a Friday."
"32","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Labid, from Ibn Sulayman ibn Yasar, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab: that he addressed the people at al-Jabiya and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as I stand among you, and said: Honor my companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then lying will spread, until a man testifies though not asked to testify, and swears though not asked to swear. Beware, let no man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Beware, whoever is pleased by the luxury of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the solitary one and is farther from two. Beware, whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer."
"33","The narrations of Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Nubayh ibn Wahb al-Hajabi informed me that he heard Aban ibn Uthman ibn Affan narrating from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one in ihram does not marry nor propose."
"34","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Nubayh ibn Wahb informed me, saying: Umar ibn Ubaydillah ibn Ma'mar complained of his eyes at Malal while in ihram, so he sent to Aban ibn Uthman ibn Affan asking him with what to treat it; and Aban ibn Uthman said to him: Bandage them with aloes, for I heard Uthman ibn Affan reporting that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: He bandages it with aloes."
"35","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from Humran, the freedman of Uthman, who said: Uthman performed ablution at the seats three times three times, and said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution; then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No man performs ablution and performs it well, then prays, except that Allah forgives him what is between it and the next prayer until he prays it."
"36","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Abu Sa'id, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, saying: Ikrima ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Dhu'bab, from his father, from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: He prayed with the people of Mina four rak'ahs, and the people disapproved of that; so he said: I took a family in it when I arrived, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man takes a family in a land, let him pray therein the prayer of a resident."
"37","The narrations of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Hasan and Abdullah, the two sons of Muhammad ibn Ali, informed me, from their father, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage and the meat of domestic donkeys at the time of Khaybar. Sufyan said: meaning he forbade the meat of domestic ones at the time of Khaybar, not meaning temporary marriage thereby."
"38","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from his father, who said: One who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying, informed me: I wanted to propose to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his daughter, then I remembered I had nothing; then I remembered his kindness and generosity, so I proposed to her. He said to me: Do you have anything to give her? I said: No. He said: Then where is your Hutamiyya armor which I gave you on such-and-such day? I said: It is with me. He said: Then bring it. He said: So I brought it and gave it to him, and he married her to me. Then when he brought her in to me he said: Do not do anything until I come to you. So he came to us while a cloak or blanket was over us; when we saw him we huddled in it, and he said: Stay in your place. Then he called for a vessel with water, supplicated in it, then sprinkled it upon us. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is she more beloved to you or I? He said: She is more beloved to me than you, and you are dearer to me than she."
"39","Abu Ali al-Sawwaf said: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Basri narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, who said: One who heard Ali ibn Abi Talib upon the minbar of Kufa informed me, and he mentioned its meaning."
"40","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn Abi Rabah informed me, saying: I heard A'ish ibn Anas saying: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib upon the minbar of Kufa saying: I suffered greatly from madhiy, and I wanted to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but his daughter was with me, so I was shy to ask him; so I commanded Ammar and he asked him, and he said: Ablution alone suffices for it."
"41","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Mutarrif ibn Tarif narrated to us: I heard al-Sha'bi saying: Abu Juhayfa informed me, saying: I said to Ali ibn Abi Talib: Do you have anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besides the Qur'an? He said: No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, except that Allah gives a servant understanding of His Book, or what is in the written sheet. I said: And what is in the صحifa? He said: Blood-money, freeing the captive, and that no Muslim is killed for a disbeliever."
"42","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla saying: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to take charge of his sacrificial camels, to distribute their coverings and hides, and not to give the butcher anything from them, saying: We shall pay him from ourselves."
"43","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to take charge of his sacrificial camels and to distribute their coverings and hides. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: Ibn Abi Najih did not add to me beyond this, but Abd al-Karim narrated it to us more completely than this."
"44","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me that he heard Mujahid saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrating from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that Fatima, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for a servant. So he said: Shall I not tell you of what is better for you than that? Glorify Allah at your bedtime thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times. Then Sufyan said: one of them is thirty-four. Ali said: I have not abandoned it since I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? He said: Not even the night of Siffin."
"45","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from his father, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that Fatima came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him for a servant, and he said: I shall not give you a servant while leaving the people of al-Suffa with their bellies folded with hunger. Shall I not tell you of what is better for you than that? Then he mentioned the like of the first hadith of Ubaydullah to its end."
"46","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Husayn narrated to us, from one who narrated to him, saying: Abdullah ibn Utba said to him: Not even the night of Siffin? He said: Not even the night of Siffin; I remembered it at the end of the night."
"47","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us that he heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymira narrating from Shurayh ibn Hani, who said: I asked A'isha about wiping over the khuffs, and she said: Go to Ali ibn Abi Talib and ask him, for he used to go out on campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I asked Ali and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: A day and a night for the resident, and three days and their nights for the traveler."
"48","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Sawda Amr al-Nahdi narrated to me, from Ibn Abd Khayr, from his father, who said: I saw Ali ibn Abi Talib wiping the upper surfaces of his two feet, saying: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping their upper surfaces, I would have thought their undersides more deserving. Abu Bakr said: If it was upon the khuffs, it is Sunna, and if it was upon other than the khuffs, it is abrogated."
"49","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Yuthay', who said: We asked Ali: With what were you sent during the Hajj? He said: I was sent with four: No soul shall enter Paradise except a believing soul; no naked person shall circumambulate the House; no Muslim and no polytheist shall gather in the Sacred Mosque after this year of theirs; and whoever had a covenant between him and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his covenant stands until its term, and whoever had no covenant, his respite is four months."
"50","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali informed me that he heard Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', the scribe of Ali ibn Abi Talib, saying: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sent me - myself, al-Zubayr and al-Miqdad - saying: Go until you reach Rawdat Khakh; there is a woman traveler with a letter, so take it from her. So we set out, our horses galloping with us, until we reached the meadow, and there was the woman traveler; we said: Bring out the letter. She said: I have no letter with me. We said: You shall bring out the letter or we shall cast off the clothes. So she brought it out from her braids, and we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and in it was: From Hatib ibn Abi Balta'a to some of the polytheists among those in Mecca, informing them of some of the affair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this, O Hatib? Hatib said: Do not hasten against me, O Messenger of Allah, for I was a man attached to Quraysh, not of themselves; and those with you of the Emigrants had relatives through whom they protected their families and wealth in Mecca, so since I lacked such lineage among them, I wished to take a favor with them through which they would protect my relatives; and I did not do it out of disbelief, nor apostasy from my religion, nor contentment with disbelief after Islam. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has told you the truth. Then Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He witnessed Badr; and what do you know - perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish, for I have forgiven you. Amr ibn Dinar said: And concerning him was revealed: O you who believe, do not take My enemy and your enemy as allies, the verse. Sufyan said: I do not know whether that is in the hadith or a statement of Amr ibn Dinar."
"51","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar Abdullah ibn Sakhbara al-Azdi, who said: They were with Ali ibn Abi Talib when a funeral passed by them, and they stood for it; so Ali said: What is this? They said: Abu Musa al-Ash'ari commanded it. So Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only stood once and did not repeat it."
"52","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Waqid ibn Amr, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam, from Ali, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only stood once, then did not repeat it. Abu Bakr al-Humaydi said: And Sufyan would sometimes narrate it to us from Ibn Abi Najih and Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar; and when we pressed him on it, he would include Abu Ma'mar in the hadith of Ibn Abi Najih, though he would not say: narrated to us, unless each of them said: narrated to us."
"53","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us: he heard it from Ibn Abi Musa, who said: I heard Ali - and he sent Abu Musa and commanded him with some of his need - and Ali said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, ask Allah for guidance and uprightness; and by guidance mean the guidance of the road, and by uprightness your aiming of the arrow. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me silk brocade and the red saddle-cloth, and that I wear my ring on this or on this - pointing to the index and middle fingers. Al-Humaydi said: And Sufyan used to narrate it from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa; then it was said to him: They only narrate it from Abu Burda. So he said: What I memorized is from Abu Bakr; but if they differ with me in it, make it from Ibn Abi Musa. So afterwards Sufyan would sometimes say: from Ibn Abi Musa, and sometimes forget and narrate it as he heard: from Abu Bakr."
"54","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan narrated to us: he heard it from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dili narrating from his father, who said: I heard Ali saying: Abdullah ibn Salam came to me when I had put my foot in the stirrup, and said to me: Where are you heading? I said: Iraq. He said: If you go to it, the edge of the sword shall strike you therein. So Ali said: By Allah, I had heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying it before him. Then Abu Harb said: I heard my father saying: I marveled at him, saying: A warrior narrating such a thing about himself."
"55","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have exempted you from the charity on horses and slaves."
"56","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that the full brothers from the same mother inherit, to the exclusion of the half-brothers from different mothers."
"57","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged that debt precedes the bequest, while you recite the bequest before the debt."
"58","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mis'ar, Ibn Abi Layla and Shu'ba, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abdullah ibn Salima, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not prevented from reciting the Qur'an except when in a state of major impurity."
"59","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Isa narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us: Adi ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: Ali ibn Abi Talib said: The unlettered Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) covenanted to me: None loves you except a believer, and none hates you except a hypocrite."
"60","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Muslim al-Abdi narrated to me: Abu Kathir narrated to us, saying: I was with my master Ali ibn Abi Talib when he fought the people of al-Nahrawan, and the people felt unease within themselves about killing them; so Ali said: O people, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me: People shall emerge from the religion as the arrow emerges from the game, never returning to it; and the sign of that is that among them is a black man with a mutilated arm, one of his arms like a woman's breast with a nipple like a woman's nipple. He said: And I think he said: Around it are seven hairs. So seek him, for I see him only among them; and they found him at the riverbank beneath the slain, and he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. And Ali was wearing an Arabian bow of his, thrusting with it at his deformed arm. He said: So the people rejoiced when they saw him and were gladdened, and what they had felt departed from them."
"61","The narrations of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: al-Zubayr said: When, Then you shall dispute before your Lord on the Day of Resurrection, was revealed, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, shall the dispute be repeated upon us after what was between us in this world? He said: Yes. So I said: Then the matter is indeed severe."
"62","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: al-Zubayr said: When, Then you shall surely be asked that Day about bliss, was revealed, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what bliss shall we be asked about? They are only the two black ones: dates and water. He said: That shall indeed come to be. Al-Humaydi said: And Sufyan would sometimes say: al-Zubayr said, and sometimes say: from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, then say: and al-Zubayr said."
"63","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Abu Damra Anas ibn Iyad al-Laythi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, who said: When, Then you shall dispute before your Lord on the Day of Resurrection, was revealed, al-Zubayr said: O Messenger of Allah, shall what was between us in this world be repeated upon us, along with the particular sins? He said: Yes, until every possessor of a right is given his right."
"64","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Insan narrated to me, from his father, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr, who said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Layya until, when we were at al-Sidra, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the edge of the black ridge facing it, gazed toward Nakhib and stood until the people gathered; then he said: The game of Wajj and its thorny trees are a sanctuary sacred to Allah. And that was before his descent upon al-Ta'if and his siege of Thaqif."
"65","The narrations of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Bajala saying: Umar would not take the jizya from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar."
"66","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Abu al-Raddad fell ill, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf visited him; and Abu al-Raddad said: The best of them and most joining - as far as I know - is Abu Muhammad. So Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah says: I am Allah and I am al-Rahman; I created the womb-tie and derived for it a name from My Name; so whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever severs it, I cut him off."
"67","The narrations of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us: Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas informed me, from his father, who said: I fell ill in Mecca in the year of the Conquest with an illness from which I was at death's door; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me visiting me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and none inherits from me except my daughter; shall I give two-thirds of my wealth in charity? He said: No. I said: Then half? He said: No. I said: Then a third? He said: A third, and a third is much; that you leave your heirs rich is better than leaving them dependent, begging from people; and you shall not spend any expenditure except that you are rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I be left behind from my emigration? He said: You shall not be left behind after me and do a deed seeking thereby Allah's Face except that you increase thereby in rank and degree; and perhaps you shall be left behind after me so that some peoples benefit by you and others are harmed by you. O Allah, complete for my companions their emigration, and do not turn them back upon their heels. But the wretched Sa'd ibn Khawla - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expressed pity for him that he died in Mecca. Sufyan said: And Sa'd ibn Khawla is a man of Banu Amir ibn Lu'ayy."
"68","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greatest of Muslims in crime against the Muslims is one who asks about a matter not forbidden, and it is then forbidden for people because of his question."
"69","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a distribution, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, give so-and-so, for he is a believer. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. Then he said: I give a man while another is dearer to me than he, fearing that Allah will cast him into the Fire."
"70","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of this hadith, adding therein: al-Zuhri said: So we consider Islam to be the word, and faith to be deeds."
"71","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiya al-Fazari and Abu Damra narrated to us, saying: Hashim ibn Hashim ibn Utba ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes seven Ajwa dates in the morning, no poison or magic shall harm him that day."
"72","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: The hadith reached me from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas; then I met Sa'd and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali ibn Abi Talib: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa?"
"73","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, saying: I heard Jabir ibn Samura al-Suwa'i saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: By Allah, the people of Kufa have complained about you in everything, even claiming you do not pray well with them. So Sa'd said: As for me, by Allah, I never fell short in leading them in the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr; I prolong the first two and shorten the last two. He said: So I heard Umar saying: That is my opinion of you; that is my opinion of you."
"74","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura, the like of it, except that he said: That is my opinion of you, O Abu Ishaq. Sufyan added therein: So Umar ordered him to be presented to the people; and he would pass no tribe but they praised him with good, until he passed a gathering of Banu Abs, and a wretched one of them, kunya Abu Sa'da, stood forth and said: I know him: he does not deal justly among the subjects, does not go out on expeditions, and does not divide equally. So Sa'd said: O Allah, if he is a liar, prolong his life, increase his children, afflict him with poverty, and put him to trial. Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr said: So I saw him as a very old man leering at slave-girls in the roads; when spoken to about that he would say: An old, poor, tempted man, struck by the supplication of the righteous man Sa'd. No trial occurs but he plunges into it."
"75","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Ala ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us that he heard Abu al-Tufayl narrating, from Bakr ibn Qirwash, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Dhu al-Thudayya and said: The devil of the pit, the keeper of the horses - or the keeper of the mountain - a man of Bajila called al-Ashhab, or Ibn al-Ashhab, brings him forth, a sign among an unjust people. Sufyan said: And Ammar al-Duhni informed me that a man of them called al-Ashhab, or Ibn al-Ashhab, brought him forth."
"76","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Umayya narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Ibn Ayyash, who said: Two men traded in the time of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, silt-grain for barley; so Sa'd said: Two men traded in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), dates for fresh dates; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Does the fresh date decrease when it dries? They said: Yes. He said: Then no."
"77","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an. Sufyan said: meaning he finds sufficiency in it."
"78","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulayka, from Abdullah ibn Abi Nahik, who said: Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas met me in the market and said: Merchants who earn, merchants who earn! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an."
"79","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim saying: I heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas saying: I am the first who shot an arrow in the path of Allah, and I remember myself with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as one of seven; and we had no food but deslab and acacia leaves, until our mouth-corners cracked, until one of us would pass droppings like a sheep passes, without mixture; then Banu Asad now rebuke me for religion. I would indeed be astray then, and my deed lost."
"80","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ya'fur narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: I prayed beside my father and clasped my hands together between my knees in bowing, and he forbade me, saying: We used to do it but were forbidden, meaning by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"81","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds each day? A questioner among his companions asked him: How does one of us earn a thousand good deeds each day? He said: He glorifies Allah a hundred times, or magnifies Him a hundred times, and they are a thousand good deeds."
"82","The narrations of Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl al-Adawi, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, saying: I heard Amr ibn Hurayth saying: I heard Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truffle is of the manna which Allah sent down upon the Children of Isra'il, and its juice is a cure for the eye."
"83","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shimmir ibn Atiya, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truffle is of the manna, its juice is a cure for the eye, and the Ajwa date - its pollinator descended from Paradise - and in it is a cure from poison."
"84","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Talha ibn Abdullah ibn Awf, the nephew of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, informed me, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land shall be collared with it from seven earths, and whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr. 83m - Al-Humaydi narrated to us: It was said to Sufyan: Ma'mar inserts a man between Talha and Sa'id. So Sufyan said: I never heard al-Zuhri insert anyone between them."
"85","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Ibn Zalim, from Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten of Quraysh are in Paradise: I am in Paradise, Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Talha is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas is in Paradise. Then Sa'id fell silent, and they said: Who is the tenth? Sa'id said: I."
"86","The narrations of Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Maymun, the freedman of the family of Samura, narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Samura, from his father, from Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Expel the Jews of the Hijaz from the Hijaz."
"87","The narrations of Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Mecca on the day of the Conquest while around the House were three hundred and sixty idols; and he began striking them with a stick in his hand, saying: Truth has come, and falsehood neither originates nor restores; Truth has come and falsehood has perished; indeed falsehood is ever perishing."
"88","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) into two halves, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness, bear witness. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: Ibn Abi Najih established for us these two hadiths from Abu Ma'mar."
"89","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: Three men gathered at the House: two Qurashis and a Thaqafi, or two Thaqafis and a Qurashi, with little understanding in their hearts and much fat in their bellies. One of them said: Do you think Allah hears what we say? Another said: He hears if we speak aloud. Another said: If He hears when we speak aloud, then He hears when we conceal. He said: So Allah revealed: You did not conceal yourselves lest your hearing, your sight testify against you, the verse. And Sufyan would first say in this hadith: Mansur narrated to us, or Ibn Abi Najih, or Humayd al-A'raj - one of them or two of them. Then he settled upon Mansur in this hadith."
"90","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us more than once, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears my saying, retains it, memorizes it and conveys it; for many a carrier of understanding is no scholar, and many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more learned than he. Three things over which a Muslim heart never harbors malice: sincerity of deed, sincere counsel to the leaders of the Muslims, and adherence to their community, for the supplication encompasses them from behind."
"91","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Jabir narrated to me that he heard Abu Majid al-Hanafi saying: I was with Abdullah when a man with a mustache was brought to him, and Abdullah said: Shake him, jostle him and make him exhale. So he was shaken and made to exhale, and behold he was drunk. So Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: Detain him. So he was detained; the next day he was brought, and I came, and Abdullah called for a whip; a whip with a knotted end was brought, and he ordered it cut off, then its tip was beaten until it became a lash for him. He said: And he signaled with his finger thus, and said to the one striking: Strike and draw back your hand, and give each limb its due; and he lashed him while he wore a shirt and waist-wrapper, and a shirt and trousers. Then Abdullah said: No holder of authority to whom a prescribed penalty is brought may but establish it; Allah is Pardoning and loves pardon. The man said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, he is my brother's son, and I have no child, and I feel for him the anguish I feel for a child. So Abdullah said: By Allah, then, what a poor guardian of the orphan you are; you neither disciplined well nor concealed the fault. Then Abdullah said: I know the first man the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ever amputated: a man of the Ansar who had stolen was brought and he amputated him, and it was as though ashes had been strewn upon the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Sufyan signaled with his palm toward his face, clutching it somewhat. They said: O Messenger of Allah, as though you disliked it. He said: And what prevents me? Do not be helpers of Satan against your brother; no holder of authority to whom a prescribed penalty is brought may but establish it, and Allah is Pardoning and loves pardon. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Let them pardon and overlook; do you not love that Allah forgive you? Sufyan said: I came to Yahya al-Jabir and he said to me: Take out your tablets. I said: I have no tablets with me; so he narrated to me this hadith and other hadiths with it, and I did not memorize this hadith until he repeated it to me. Sufyan said: So I memorized it from two hearings."
"92","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us - and we had met him in Mecca - saying: I entered upon Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami visiting him when sick, and a slave of his wanted to treat him, but I forbade him; so he said: Leave him, for I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud reporting from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah sent down no disease but He sent down for it a remedy. And Sufyan would sometimes say: a cure - whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"93","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: What Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: Keep to this Qur'an, for it escapes from men's chests more swiftly than camels from their halters. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil is it for one of them to say: I forgot such-and-such verse; rather, he was made to forget."
"94","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Mansur narrated to us, saying: Dharr al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Wa'il ibn Muhana, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity, O company of women, even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire. A woman - not of the eminent women - stood and said: Why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Because you curse much and are ungrateful to the husband. Then Abdullah said: None of deficient intellect and religion was found more overpowering over resolute men in their affairs than women. He said: It was said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is her deficiency of intellect and religion? He said: As for her deficiency of intellect: Allah made the testimony of two women equal to the testimony of one man; and as for her deficiency of religion: she stays so many days without praying to Allah a single prostration."
"95","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Jami' ibn Abi Rashid and Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one who withholds the zakat of his wealth but a bald serpent shall be formed for him, collaring him on the Day of Resurrection. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited its confirmation from the Book of Allah: Let not those who withhold what Allah has given them of His bounty think it good for them; rather it is evil for them; they shall be collared with what they withheld on the Day of Resurrection, the verse."
"96","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: We used to greet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer before we came to the land of Abyssinia, and he would return it to us; then when we returned I greeted him while he was praying and he did not return it to me, and I was seized by near and far distress; so I sat until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, and I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I greeted you while you were praying and you did not return the greeting to me. So he said: Allah introduces into His affair what He wills, and of what He introduced is that you not speak in prayer. Sufyan said: This is the best we found with Asim in this version."
"97","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan and Jami' ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off a Muslim man's wealth with a lying oath shall meet Allah while He is angry with him. Abdullah said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to us its confirmation from the Book of Allah Most High: Those who purchase with Allah's covenant and their oaths, the verse."
"98","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mansur narrated to us more than once this hadith, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, that Abdullah ibn Mas'ud performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salutation, and narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed them after the salutation. Sufyan said: It was long, and this is what I memorized of it."
"99","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, that a woman of Banu Asad came to Ibn Mas'ud and said to him: It reached me that you cursed so-and-so, and the woman who tattoos and the woman who has herself tattooed; and I have read what is between the two covers yet did not find what you say, though I suspect some of your household practice it. So Abdullah said to her: Then enter and look. So she entered and looked and saw nothing. He said: So Abdullah said to her: Have you not read: Whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, abstain? She said: Yes. He said: Then it is that."
"100","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim al-Hajari Abu Ishaq narrated to us that he heard Abu al-Ahwas saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan has despaired that idols be worshipped in this land of yours - or in this town of yours - but he is content with the belittled deeds among your deeds; so beware of belittled deeds, for they are of the ruinous ones. Shall I not tell you the like of that? The like of riders who alight in a barren land with no firewood, then scatter: one brings a stick, one brings a bone, one brings dung, until they cook what they intended; so too are sins."
"101","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us this hadith differently from how al-Zuhri narrated it to us, saying: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah gave wealth and empowered him to spend it away in truth, and a man to whom Allah gave wisdom, and he judges by it or teaches it."
"102","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us that he heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: We used to go out on campaigns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without women with us, and we wanted to castrate ourselves, but he forbade us that."
"103","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: Recite. He said: Shall I recite while it was revealed to you? He said: I love to hear it from other than myself. He said: So I recited Surat al-Nisa until, when I reached: How shall it be when We bring from every nation a witness and bring you against these as a witness, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept, and Abdullah stopped."
"104","Sufyan said: al-Mas'udi said: And Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Hurayth narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A witness over them while I am among them; then when You took me, You were the Watcher over them, and You are Witness over all things."
"105","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard an old man of al-Nakha' named Amr, kunya Abu Mu'awiya, saying: I heard Abu Amr al-Shaybani saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deed is most excellent? He said: Faith in Allah and striving in His path. I said: Then which? He said: Then prayer at its time. I said: Then which? He said: Then kindness to parents. I said: Then which of the major sins is gravest? He said: That you set up a rival to Allah while He created you. I said: Then which? He said: That you kill your child lest he eat with you. I said: Then which? He said: Then that you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And those who do not call upon another god with Allah, nor kill the soul Allah forbade except by right, nor commit adultery; and whoever does that shall meet punishment, the verse."
"106","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reviling the Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"107","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, who said: I entered with my father upon Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, and my father said to him: Did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Remorse is repentance? So Abdullah said: Yes; I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Remorse is repentance."
"108","Sufyan said: And Abu Sa'd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it. And what Abd al-Karim narrated to us is dearer to me, for he is more retentive than Abu Sa'd."
"109","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a cave when there was revealed to him: By those sent forth in succession; so I took it from his mouth while his mouth was still moist with it, and I do not know with which of the two he sealed: Then in what narration after it shall they believe, or: And when it is said to them, Bow, they do not bow. He said: And a snake emerged upon us from a hole and eluded us, entering another hole; so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You were spared its evil, and it was spared your evil."
"110","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Wa'il Shaqiq ibn Salama saying: We were sitting awaiting Abdullah ibn Mas'ud when Yazid ibn Mu'awiya al-Nakha'i came to us and said: What is the matter with you? We said: We await Abdullah ibn Mas'ud. He said: Where do you think he is? We said: In the house. He said: Shall I not go and bring him out to you? So he went, and before long Abdullah came out until he stood over us, with Yazid ibn Mu'awiya; and Abdullah said: I am informed of your gathering, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except dislike of boring you; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose the suitable time for admonishing us in the days, disliking weariness for us."
"111","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-A'mash saying: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf saying: Do not say Surat al-Baqara, nor such-and-such sura. So I mentioned it to Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i, and he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid informed me that he walked with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud in the valley's bottom; and when he reached the jamra he put it to his right, then faced it and stoned it. I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, people stone it from above it. He said: From here - by the One besides whom there is no god - I saw the one to whom Surat al-Baqara was revealed stone it."
"112","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Two men should not converse privately to the exclusion of a third, for that grieves him."
"113","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a distribution, and a man said: This is a distribution by which the Face of Allah was not intended. 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: I could not restrain myself from going to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informing him, and his face changed. 'Abdullah said: I then wished I had only become Muslim that day. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Musa was harmed with worse than this, and he was patient."
"114","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-A'mash saying: I heard al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf saying: Do not say Surah al-Baqarah, nor Surah so-and-so. I mentioned it to Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i, and he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid informed me that he walked with 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud in the valley bottom, and when he came to the Jamrah he put it on his right, then faced it across from it and stoned it. I said to him: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, some people stone it from above it. He said: From here, by the One besides whom there is no god, I saw the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed stone it."
"115","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, he said: 'Abdullah came to Sham and recited Surah Yusuf, and a man said to him: It was not revealed like this. 'Abdullah said: Woe to you, I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: You did well. While he was disputing with him, 'Abdullah noticed the smell of wine from him, so 'Abdullah said: Do you drink wine and deny the Qur'an? I will not move until you are flogged. So he was flogged."
"116","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us more than once, from 'Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I dissociate myself before every close friend from his intimate friendship, and had I taken an intimate friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, and your Companion is the intimate friend of Allah, meaning himself."
"117","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer except at its time, except at Muzdalifah, for he joined the two prayers, Maghrib and 'Isha, and he prayed the morning prayer that day before its time. Sufyan said: meaning before the time at which he used to pray it before that."
"118","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: O company of young men, whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity, and whoever cannot, let him fast, for fasting is a restraint for him."
"119","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash, or it was reported to me from him, from Muslim ibn Subayh, meaning from Masruq, he said: It was said to 'Abdullah: There is a man in the mosque saying: When the Day of Resurrection comes, people will be struck by a smoke that seizes the disbelievers by their hearing, and seizes the believers like a cold. 'Abdullah was reclining, then he sat up and said: O people, whoever among you knows something, let him say it, and whoever does not know, let him say for what he does not know: Allah knows best, for part of a man's knowledge is to say for what he does not know: Allah knows best. Allah said to His Prophet: Say: I ask you for it no reward, and I am not of those who affect. When Quraysh were slow against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Allah, help me against them with seven like the seven of Yusuf. A famine struck them that consumed everything, until they ate bones, and a man would look at the sky and see between him and it something like smoke. Allah Almighty said: So watch for the day the sky brings a clear smoke, covering the people; this is a painful punishment. Allah said: We shall remove the punishment a little; you will return. This was in this world; will it be removed from them on the Day of Resurrection? Then 'Abdullah said: The smoke has passed, and the inevitability has passed, and the moon has passed, and the Romans have passed, and the mighty seizure has passed."
"120","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, he said: We were with Masruq in the house of Yasar ibn Numayr, and Masruq saw images in his gallery, so he said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers."
"121","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash, from 'Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No soul is killed unjustly except that upon the first son of Adam is a share of it, because he first instituted killing."
"122","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except in one of three: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, or commits adultery after being married, or a life for a life."
"123","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: We asked about that, meaning the souls of the martyrs, and it was said: They are placed in the bellies of green birds that shelter at lamps beneath the Throne, roaming in Paradise wherever they wish. Your Lord looked upon them and said: Do you want Me to increase you in anything so I increase you? They said: What more would we want of You, while we are in Paradise roaming in it wherever we wish? Then your Lord looked upon them again and said: Do you want Me to increase you in anything so I increase you? When they saw that they must ask Him, they said: Return our souls into our bodies so we may be killed in Your path once more."
"124","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Abu 'Ubaydah, from 'Abdullah, similar to it. And he added: And convey to our Prophet greetings of peace from us, and inform our people that we are pleased and He is pleased with us."
"125","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Shimmar ibn 'Atiyyah, from al-Mughirah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Akhram, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Do not take estates, lest you become attached to this world. Then 'Abdullah said: And Baradhan, what is Baradhan, and Madinah, what is Madinah. [Flag: fragmentary local remark, literal rendering.]"
"126","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mis'ar, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu 'Ubaydah, he said: Masruq said to me: Your father informed me that a tree warned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the jinn. [Flag: terse and ambiguous in the source, rendered literally.]"
"127","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mis'ar, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Salamah, from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: Your Prophet was given knowledge of everything except five: Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, to the end of the surah."
"128","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Murrah, from 'Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Mughirah al-Yashkuri, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: Umm Habibah said: O Allah, grant me enjoyment through my husband the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and through my father Abu Sufyan, and through my brother Mu'awiyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have asked Allah for fixed terms, and allotted spans, and apportioned provisions; nothing of them comes before its term, and nothing of them is delayed beyond its time. Had you asked Allah to save you from punishment in the Fire and punishment in the grave, it would have been better. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about monkeys and pigs: do you think they are from the descendants of those who were transformed, or from creatures before that? He said: No, rather from creatures before that. Allah Almighty never destroys a people and then gives them descendants or posterity; rather they are from creatures before that."
"129","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, and he is the truthful one believed: One of you has his creation gathered in his mother's womb for forty days, then he is a clot like that, then he is a lump like that, then Allah sends to him the angel with four words, saying: Write his deed, and his term, and whether wretched or blessed. Then the spirit is breathed into him. Then he said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, a man does the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the decree overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise and enters it. And a man does the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the decree overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it."
"130","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah, that he said: None of you should give Satan a share of his prayer, thinking it binding upon him not to leave except to his right, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often leave to his left."
"131","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating that he heard Abu Dharr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you stands for prayer, mercy faces him, so let him not wipe the pebbles. Sufyan said: Sa'd ibn Ibrahim said to him: Who is Abu al-Ahwas? As if angry at him for narrating from an unknown man he did not know. Al-Zuhri said to him: Do you not know the shaykh, the freedman of Banu Ghifar, who used to pray in the Rawdah? And he described him to him, while Sa'd did not know him."
"132","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ju'dubah al-Laythi informed me that he heard 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mikhraq narrating from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah created in Paradise a wind after a wind seven years later, and before it is a closed door, and the wind comes to you only through the opening of that door. Had it been opened, it would scatter everything between heaven and earth, and with Allah it is al-Azyab, and among you it is the south wind. [Flag: obscure wording, rendered literally.]"
"133","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to Muhammad ibn al-Sa'ib ibn Barakah: Did you see 'Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi? He said: Yes, he used to stay with us. I said: Did you hear anything from him? He said: Yes, I heard 'Amr ibn Maymun saying: I heard Abu Dharr saying: I was walking behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me: O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to a treasure among the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"134","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Abu Murawih al-Ghifari, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Faith in Allah, and striving in the path of Allah. He said: I said: Which necks are best to free? He said: The most expensive in price and the most precious to their owners. I said: If I cannot do that? He said: Then you help a craftsman, or do work for one who cannot work skillfully. I said: If I cannot do that? He said: Then you withhold your harm from people, for it is a charity you give on behalf of yourself."
"135","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Muraqqa', from Abu Dharr, he said: The annulment of Hajj was from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for us specifically."
"136","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn 'Asim ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi narrated to us from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of wealth have surpassed us in reward; they say as we say, and they spend while we do not spend. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to a deed, when you say it you catch up with those before you, and those after you cannot surpass you except one who says as you say? Glorify Allah after every prayer thirty-three times, praise Allah thirty-three times, and magnify Allah thirty-four times. Al-Humaydi said: Then Sufyan said: One of them is thirty-four: and at your bedtime likewise."
"137","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: I was walking with my father when he recited the prostration verse and prostrated, then he said: I heard Abu Dharr saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was first placed on the face of the earth? He said: The Sacred Mosque. I said: Then which? He said: The Furthest Mosque. I said: How long between them? He said: Forty years. I said: Then which? He said: Then wherever prayer reaches you, pray, for the whole earth is a mosque."
"138","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Muraqqa', from Abu Dharr, that he said: The annulment of Hajj was from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for us specifically."
"139","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talhah, and Hakim ibn Jubayr narrated to us, both heard it from Musa ibn Talhah: that he heard a man from his maternal uncles of Banu Tamim called Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah saying: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Who of us was present on the day of al-Qahah, when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a rabbit? Abu Dharr said: I was. A Bedouin brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a rabbit and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw it bleeding. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refrained from it and did not eat, and ordered his Companions to eat, while the Bedouin kept apart and did not eat, saying: I am fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is your fast? He said: Three days of every month. He said: Where are you with regard to the white shining days: the thirteenth, the fourteenth, and the fifteenth?"
"140","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from 'Amr ibn 'Uthman, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it, except he did not mention Ibn al-Hawtakiyyah in it."
"141","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, I think, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn Wadi'ah, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes and bathes well on Friday, or purifies himself and purifies well, then wears some of his good clothes, and touches whatever Allah has decreed for him of his family's perfume, then goes to Friday prayer without separating two people, he is forgiven what is between the two Fridays plus three days more."
"142","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Samad al-'Ammi narrated to us, he said: Abu 'Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr, when you cook, increase the broth and look after your neighbors, or share with your neighbors."
"143","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him saying: They are the lowest, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. I said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The most wealthy, except one who says with wealth: like this and like this and like this, and few are they."
"144","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from 'Asim ibn 'Ubaydullah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) countless times using the tooth-stick while fasting."
"145","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn 'Abdullah informed me, from his father, from 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the funeral bier, stand for it until it leaves you behind or is placed down."
"146","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Utbah, from his father, from 'Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: We performed dry ablution with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) up to the shoulders. Abu Bakr said: I was present with Sufyan when Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan asked him about it, and he narrated it to him, saying in it: al-Zuhri narrated to us. Then he said: I was present when Isma'il ibn Umayyah came to al-Zuhri and said: O Abu Bakr, people object to two hadiths you narrate. He said: What are they? He said: We performed dry ablution with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) up to the shoulders. Al-Zuhri said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abdullah informed me, from his father, from 'Ammar. He said: And the hadith of 'Umar that he ordered ablution from touching the armpit. I saw al-Zuhri as if he disapproved of it, though 'Amr ibn Dinar had narrated it to us from al-Zuhri before that; I mentioned it to 'Amr, and he said: Yes, he did narrate it to us."
"147","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Khufaf, Najiyah ibn Ka'b, he said: 'Ammar said to 'Umar: Do you not remember when you and I were with the camels and I became ritually impure, so I rolled in the dust as an animal rolls, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we mentioned that to him, and he said: Dry ablution alone would have sufficed you for that."
"148","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from a man of Banu Sulaym, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Anamah al-Juhani, that a man saw 'Ammar ibn Yasir praying a prayer he shortened, and when he finished he said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you prayed a prayer you shortened. He said: Did you see me omit anything from its bowing and prostration? He said: No. He said: I hastened against forgetfulness, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man prays a prayer and leaves, and nothing is recorded for him of it except a tenth of it, a ninth, an eighth, a sixth, a fifth, a quarter, a third, a half."
"149","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from 'Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from Hassan ibn Bilal al-Muzani, he said: 'Ammar ibn Yasir was seen performing ablution while running his fingers through his beard. It was said to him: Do you run your fingers through your beard? He said: What prevents me, when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running his fingers through his beard?"
"150","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah, from Qatadah, from Hassan ibn Bilal, from 'Ammar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"151","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us at Mina, he said: Ibn 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to the mosque of Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf at Quba to pray in it, and some men of the Ansar came to him greeting him. I asked Suhayb, who was with him: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) return their greetings when they greeted him while he was praying? Suhayb said: He would gesture to them with his hand. Sufyan said: I said to a man: Ask him: Did you hear it from Ibn 'Umar? He said: O Abu Usamah, did you hear it from Ibn 'Umar? He said: As for me, I spoke to him and he spoke to me, but he did not say: I heard it from him."
"152","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I said to Bilal: Where did he pray in the House? He said: Between the two front pillars. And I forgot to ask him: How many did he pray?"
"153","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Taghlib and Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Bilal, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the two leather socks and the head-cover."
"154","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from 'Amr, from Yahya ibn Ja'dah, he said: Some people visited Khabbab to see him when ill, and said: Rejoice, O Abu 'Abdullah, you will meet Muhammad at the Basin. He said: What about this and this? Pointing to his building, the ceiling of the house and its sides, and said: What about this, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: One of you needs of this world only like the provision of a rider."
"155","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the heat of the sun-baked ground, and he did not relieve our complaint."
"156","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the sun-baked ground, and he did not relieve our complaint."
"157","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, he said: We visited Khabbab when he had been cauterized seven times on his stomach, and he said: Had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not forbidden us to pray for death, I would have prayed for it. Then he said: People before us passed who attained nothing of this world, while we remained after them and attained of this world so much that none of us knows in what he places it except in dust. A Muslim is rewarded for everything he spends except what he spends in dust."
"158","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il saying: We visited Khabbab to see him when ill, and he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking the Face of Allah, so our reward fell upon Allah. Some of us passed without consuming anything of their reward, among them Mus'ab ibn 'Umayr, killed on the day of Uhud, leaving a striped woolen cloak; when we covered his feet his head showed, and when we covered his head his feet showed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to cover his head and to put some idhkhir grass on his feet. And some of us had their fruit ripen for them, and they are gathering it."
"159","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, he said: We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and 'Asr? He said: Yes. We said: By what did you recognize that? He said: By the movement of his beard."
"160","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Bayan ibn Bishr and Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, both said: We heard Qays saying: I heard Khabbab saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was pillowing his cloak in the shade of the Ka'bah, and we had met severe hardship from the polytheists. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate to Allah for us? He sat up with his face reddened and said: Among those before you, one of them would be combed with iron combs, flesh or sinew beneath his bone, yet that did not turn him from his religion. A saw would be placed on the parting of his head and split into two, yet that did not turn him from his religion. Allah will complete this matter until a rider travels from San'a to Hadramawt fearing none but Allah. Bayan added: And the wolf against his sheep."
"161","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Mis'ar, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: The remaining Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Khabbab in his illness, and said: Rejoice, O Abu 'Abdullah, you will meet your brothers at the Basin. He said: And upon it are men. You have mentioned to me peoples, and named brothers to me who passed without attaining anything of their rewards, while we remained after them and attained of this world what we fear may be the reward for those deeds."
"162","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: I heard 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bathe in the cup, which is the faraq, and I and he would bathe from a single vessel."
"163","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, that Umm Habibah bint Jahsh suffered prolonged bleeding for seven years, and she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: That is only a vein, and it is not menstruation. He ordered her to bathe and pray. She would bathe for every prayer, and sit in the washbasin while the blood rose above it."
"164","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr performed ablution in the presence of 'A'ishah, and she said: Perform ablution fully, O 'Abd al-Rahman, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Woe to the heels from the Fire."
"165","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Atiq, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tooth-stick is a purification for the mouth and a means of pleasing the Lord."
"166","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to bathe from major impurity, he would begin by washing his hands before putting them into the vessel, then wash his private part, then perform his ablution for prayer, then soak his hair with water, then pour three handfuls over his head."
"167","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: Children were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would supplicate for them. A boy was brought, and he urinated upon him, so he followed his urine with water."
"168","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that her necklace fell on the night of al-Abwa. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent two Muslim men to seek it. Prayer came while they had no water with them, and they did not know what to do. The verse of dry ablution was revealed. Usayd ibn Hudayr said: May Allah reward you with good; never has a matter befallen you that you disliked except that Allah made for you a way out of it, and made in it good for the Muslims."
"169","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give me the bone while I was menstruating, and I would gnaw it, then he would take it and turn it until he placed his mouth upon the place of my mouth."
"170","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hajabi narrated to us, he said: My mother informed me that she heard 'A'ishah saying: A woman asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about bathing from menstruation. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take a piece of cotton with musk and purify yourself with it. She said: How shall I purify myself with it? He said: Purify yourself with it. She said: I said: How shall I purify myself with it? He gestured with his hand like this: Glory be to Allah, purify yourself with it? And he covered himself with his garment. 'A'ishah said: I understood what he meant, so I drew her aside and said to her: Follow with it the traces of blood."
"171","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Mu'adhah al-'Adawiyyah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would bathe from a single vessel, and he would sometimes say to me: Leave some for me, leave some for me."
"172","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: My mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah informed me, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his head in the lap of one of us and recite the Qur'an while she was menstruating."
"173","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray 'Asr while the sun was still high in my chamber, before the shade had appeared over it."
"174","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray his night prayer while I lay across between him and the qiblah, like the lying of a funeral bier."
"175","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a woolen garment with marks, and said: Its marks distracted me; take it to Abu Jahm and bring me his plain cloak."
"176","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Abdullah ibn Abi Labid, one of the worshippers of the people of Madinah, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman saying: I visited 'A'ishah and said: O mother, inform me about the night prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and about his fasting. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until we said he has fasted continuously, and break fast until we said he has broken fast. I never saw him fasting in any month more than his fasting in Sha'ban; he would fast it all, indeed he would fast it except a little. His night prayer in Ramadan and otherwise was thirteen rak'ahs, including the two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"177","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: Believing women would pray Fajr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrapped in their woolen shawls, then return to their families, unrecognized by anyone because of the darkness."
"178","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr; if I was awake he would talk to me, otherwise he would lie down until he rose for the prayer."
"179","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Ibn Abi 'Attab, from Abu Salamah, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"180","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah al-Laythi narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray his night prayer while I lay across between him and the qiblah. When he intended to pray witr he would move me with his foot. He would pray the two rak'ahs; if I was awake he would talk to me, otherwise he would lie down until he rose for the prayer. Sufyan would doubt the hadith of Abu al-Nadr, wavering in it, and sometimes doubt the hadith of Ziyad, saying: It gets mixed up for me. Then he told us more than once: The hadith of Abu al-Nadr is such, and the hadith of Ziyad is such, and the hadith of Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Alqamah is such, as I mentioned, all of that."
"181","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us countless times, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: People used to work for themselves, and they would come on Friday in their work clothes. It was said to them: If only you would bathe."
"182","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id saying: I heard 'Amrah narrating from 'A'ishah, that she said: A Jewish woman came and said: May Allah protect you from the punishment of the grave. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will we be punished in our graves? He said a word of seeking refuge in Allah from that. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day on a mount, and the sun eclipsed. I went out with some women between the chambers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came quickly from his mount until he stood at his place of prayer. He magnified Allah and stood a long standing, then bowed a long bowing, then rose and stood a long standing, shorter than the first standing, then bowed a long bowing, shorter than the first bowing, then rose, then prostrated a long prostration, then rose, then prostrated a long prostration, shorter than the first prostration. Then he did in the second the same. His prayer was four bowings and four prostrations. She said: I heard him after that seeking refuge from the punishment of the grave, saying: You will be tried in your graves like the trial of the Messiah, or like the trial of the Dajjal."
"183","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it concerning four bowings in four prostrations. Sufyan said: And he mentioned nothing else."
"184","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr so lightly that I would say: Did he recite in them the Opening of the Book?"
"185","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is served and prayer is established, begin with supper."
"186","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Salamah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a mat he would spread by day, and at night he would make it into a chamber and pray in it. Some people followed him praying with his prayer. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) noticed them, so he left that, and said: I feared something would be imposed concerning them that they could not bear. Then he said: Take on of deeds what you can bear, for Allah does not tire until you tire. He said: The most beloved deed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was what was done consistently, even if little, and when he prayed a prayer he kept to it."
"187","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in retreat in the mosque and extended his head to me, and I washed it while I was menstruating."
"188","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes while praying, let him leave, for he does not know; perhaps he intends to seek forgiveness but curses himself. Or he said: Then he supplicates against himself."
"189","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Hammam, he said: A guest stayed with 'A'ishah, so she sent for him inviting him. They said to her: He became ritually impure and went to wash his garment. 'A'ishah said: Why wash it? I used to rub semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"190","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ya'fur ibn 'Ubayd ibn Nistas narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, she said: When the last ten of Ramadan entered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake his family, keep the night alive, and tighten his waist-wrapper. He said: Another said: And exert himself."
"191","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ya'fur ibn 'Ubayd ibn Nistas narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr at every part of the night, and his witr ended at dawn."
"192","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from 'A'ishah, that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never found the last dawn with me except sleeping."
"193","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his paternal aunt 'A'ishah bint Talhah, from her maternal aunt 'A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me and said: Is there any food? I said: Yes, and I brought near to him a cup containing hays we had stored for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his hand and ate, and said: I had been fasting."
"194","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his paternal aunt 'A'ishah bint Talhah, from her maternal aunt 'A'ishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me one day and said: Is there any food? I said: We have no food. He said: Then I am fasting."
"195","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray at night standing. When he grew old he prayed sitting; when thirty or forty verses remained upon him, he would stand, recite them, then bow."
"196","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh suffered prolonged bleeding, and she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to her: It is only a vein, and it is not menstruation. When menstruation comes, leave prayer, and when it goes, bathe and pray. Or he said: Wash the blood from yourself and pray."
"197","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never omitted the two rak'ahs after 'Asr with me."
"198","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr with five, sitting only in the last of them."
"199","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id narrating from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to observe retreat in the last ten of Ramadan. I heard of that and asked his permission, and he permitted me. Then Hafsah asked his permission, and he permitted her. Then Zaynab asked his permission, and he permitted her. She said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended retreat, he would pray Fajr then enter his place of retreat. When he prayed Fajr he saw four structures in the mosque, and said: What is this? They said: For 'A'ishah and Hafsah and Zaynab. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do they intend righteousness by this? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not observe retreat in those ten, and observed retreat for ten in Shawwal. Abu Bakr said: Sometimes Sufyan would say in this hadith: Do you call it righteousness with them?"
"200","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, he said: We set out as pilgrims, and the people discussed: may a fasting person kiss? A man among the people said: Yes. Another, who had fasted two years and stood their nights, said: I felt like taking this bow of mine and striking you with it. When we reached Madinah we visited 'A'ishah, and they said: O Abu Shibl, ask her. I said: By Allah, I will not utter anything indecent before her all day. She heard their talk and said: What were you saying? I am only your mother. They said: O Mother of the Believers, may a fasting person kiss? 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss and embrace while fasting, and he had the most control of you over his desire."
"201","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim: Did you hear your father narrating from 'A'ishah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss her while fasting? He was silent for a while, then said: Yes."
"202","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss some of his wives while fasting. Then she laughed."
"203","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman saying: I heard 'A'ishah saying: Dawn would reach the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in major impurity, then he would bathe and fast that day."
"204","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, that Hamzah ibn 'Amr al-Aslami, who would fast continuously, said: O Messenger of Allah, I fast continuously; shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast, and if you wish, break fast."
"205","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Both al-Zuhri and Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: The day of 'Ashura was a day fasted in the pre-Islamic age before the month of Ramadan was revealed. When the month of Ramadan was revealed, whoever wished fasted it and whoever wished did not fast it."
"206","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: Safiyyah bint Huyayy menstruated after performing the farewell circumambulation. I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Will she detain us? I said: O Messenger of Allah, she menstruated after performing the farewell circumambulation. He said: Then let her depart."
"207","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it, except that he said: Then no, never mind."
"208","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Whoever of you wishes to enter ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah, let him enter ihram, and whoever wishes to enter ihram for Hajj, let him enter ihram, and whoever wishes to enter ihram for 'Umrah, let him enter ihram. 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj, and some people with him entered ihram for it, and some people entered ihram for 'Umrah, and I was among those who entered ihram for 'Umrah. Sufyan said: Then the hadith overcame me; this is what I retained of it."
"209","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: 'Alqamah informed me, from his mother, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you wishes to enter ihram for 'Umrah, let him do so. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj alone and did not perform 'Umrah."
"210","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah, Anas ibn 'Iyad al-Laythi, narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad, Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, orphan of 'Urwah, narrated to me, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, that she said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Some of us performed Hajj alone, some combined, and some performed 'Umrah. As for whoever circumambulated the House and ran between Safa and Marwah, he exited ihram; as for whoever performed Hajj alone or combined, he did not exit ihram until stoning the Jamrah."
"211","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father informed me that he heard 'A'ishah saying: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his Hajj, thinking of nothing but Hajj. When I was at Sarif or near it, I menstruated. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was weeping, and said: What is wrong with you? Have you menstruated? I said: Yes. He said: This is a matter Allah has decreed for the daughters of Adam, so perform what the pilgrim performs, except that you do not circumambulate the House. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed cows on behalf of his wives."
"212","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Amrah, from 'A'ishah, she said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with five nights remaining of Dhu al-Qa'dah, thinking of nothing but Hajj. When we were at Sarif or near it, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered whoever had no sacrificial animal with him to make it 'Umrah. When we were at Mina, beef was brought to me, and I said: What is this? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered cows on behalf of his wives. Yahya said: I narrated it to al-Qasim, and he said: By Allah, she brought you the hadith correctly."
"213","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I would twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these hands of mine, then he would not avoid anything that a person in ihram avoids."
"214","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, informing from his father, from 'A'ishah, she said: I would twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these hands of mine, then he would not keep away from anything a person in ihram keeps away from, nor leave it. 'A'ishah said: And we know nothing makes the pilgrim lawful except circumambulation of the House."
"215","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, he said: I heard 'A'ishah, spreading her hand, saying: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these hands of mine for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his exiting ihram before he circumambulated the House. Abu Bakr said: This is what we adopt."
"216","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, she said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these hands of mine for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his exiting ihram before he circumambulated the House. Abu Bakr said: This is among what Sufyan did not used to narrate from al-Zuhri in early times; we stopped him at it, and he said: I heard it from al-Zuhri."
"217","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Salim ibn 'Abdullah, from his father, he said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said: When you stone the Jamrah, slaughter, and shave, everything forbidden to you becomes lawful except women and perfume. Salim ibn 'Abdullah said: 'A'ishah said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his exiting ihram after he stoned the Jamrah and before he visited the House. Salim said: The practice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is most worthy to be followed."
"218","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Uthman ibn 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: My father informed me that he heard 'A'ishah saying: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his ihram and for his exiting ihram. I said: With what perfume? She said: With the best perfume."
"219","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan said: 'Uthman ibn 'Urwah said to me: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrates this hadith only from me."
"220","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from 'A'ishah, that she said: I saw the glisten of perfume in the partings of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after three days, while he was in ihram. [Flag: source phrase compact; rendered literally.]"
"221","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir narrated to us, from his father, he said: I asked Ibn 'Umar about perfume for a person in ihram at his ihram. He said: I do not like to enter the morning in ihram with the scent of perfume exuding from me; rubbing tar would be dearer to me than it. My father said: One of the sons of 'Abdullah sent to 'A'ishah so his father could hear what she said. The messenger came and said: She said: I perfumed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn 'Umar fell silent."
"222","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once sent sheep as sacrificial animals. Al-Humaydi said: Abu Mu'awiyah added for me in it: And he garlanded them."
"223","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aisha, who said: I used to twist the garlands of the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from sheep’s wool, then he would not avoid anything that the one in pilgrim sanctity avoids."
"224","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating, from Urwah, who said: I recited in the presence of Aisha: {Indeed, as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah; whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to circumambulate them.} So I said: I would not care if I did not circumambulate them. She said: What an evil thing you have said, O son of my sister! It was only that those who entered ihram for Manat, the false deity at al-Mushallal, would not circumambulate between as-Safa and al-Marwah, so Allah revealed: {Indeed, as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah; whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to circumambulate them.} So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated, and the Muslims circumambulated. Sufyan said: And Mujahid said: So it became a sunnah. Al-Zuhri said: So I narrated it to Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he said: This is knowledge indeed; I have heard men of knowledge saying: Those among the Arabs who would not circumambulate between as-Safa and al-Marwah would say: Our circumambulation between these two stones is from the affairs of the pre-Islamic ignorance. And others among the Ansar said: We were only commanded to circumambulate the House, and we were not commanded to circumambulate between as-Safa and al-Marwah. So Allah revealed: {Indeed, as-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah.} Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman said: Perhaps it was revealed concerning these and those."
"225","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, that he heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah saying: I attended the funeral of Umm Aban bint Uthman, and in the funeral were Abdullah ibn Umar and Abdullah ibn Abbas, so I sat between them, and the women wept. So Ibn Umar said: The weeping of the living over the dead is torment for the dead. He said: So Ibn Abbas said: We set out with Umar, the Commander of the Believers, until when we were at al-Bayda, he saw riders dismounted under a tree, and said: Go, O Abdullah, and see who the riders are, then join me. He said: So I went, then I came back and said: This is Suhayb, the freed slave of Ibn Jud’an. He said: Tell him to join me. When they arrived at Madinah, Umar had not remained long before he was stabbed, so Suhayb came saying: O my brother! O my companion! So Umar said: Hush, O Suhayb! The dead is tormented by the weeping of the living over him. Ibn Abbas said: So I went to Aisha and asked her, and she said: May Allah have mercy on Umar; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: “Allah increases the torment of the disbeliever because of some of his family’s weeping over him.” And Allah has decreed: {No bearer of burdens shall bear the burden of another.}"
"226","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to us, from his father, from Amrah, that she heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said concerning a Jewish woman, while they were weeping over her: “Her family are now weeping over her, while she is being tormented in her grave.”"
"227","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, the foster brother of Aisha, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is no dead person over whom a community of people reaching one hundred pray and intercede for him, except that their intercession for him is accepted.”"
"228","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Madinah, his Companions were struck with fever, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abu Bakr to console him and said: “How do you find yourself, O Abu Bakr?” So Abu Bakr said [in fragmentary verse]: “Musabbahun shiraki.” And he visited Amir ibn Fuhayrah and said: “How do you find yourself?” So he said [in fragmentary verse]: “Hatfuhu.” She said: And he visited Bilal and said: “How do you find yourself?” So he said [in fragmentary verse]: “Bi-fakhkhin idhkhirun.” He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and Your intimate friend; he supplicated You for the people of Makkah, and I am Your servant and Your Messenger; I supplicate You for the people of Madinah with the like of what he supplicated You for the people of Makkah. O Allah, bless for us our sa’, bless for us our mudd, and bless for us our city.” Sufyan said: And I see in it: “and in our faraq”: “O Allah, make it beloved to us as You made Makkah beloved to us, or more so; make it healthy, and transfer its plague and its fever to Khumm, or to al-Juhfah.”"
"229","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: “They now know that what I used to tell them in this world is true.” And Allah has said to His Prophet: {Indeed, you cannot make the dead hear.}"
"230","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za’idah, from al-Sha’bi, from Shurayh ibn Hani, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever dislikes meeting Allah, Allah dislikes meeting him.” And meeting Him (meeting Allah) is after death."
"231","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Urwah informed me, from Aisha, that he heard her saying: The wife of Rifa’ah al-Qurazi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I was with Rifa’ah al-Qurazi and he divorced me with a final divorce, then I married Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, and what is with him is like this fringe. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: “Do you wish to return to Rifa’ah? No, until you taste his little honey and he tastes your little honey.” She said: And Abu Bakr was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Khalid ibn Sa’id ibn al-As was at the door waiting to be admitted, so he called out: O Abu Bakr, do you not hear what this woman openly says in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? It was said to Sufyan: Malik does not narrate it from al-Zuhri; he only narrates it from al-Miswar ibn Rifa’ah. So Sufyan said: But we heard it from al-Zuhri as we narrated it to you."
"232","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Aisha, that she narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except over a husband.” So it was said to Sufyan: But she mourns over him for four months and ten days? So Sufyan said: al-Zuhri did not tell us this in his hadith; Ayyub ibn Musa told it to us in his hadith."
"233","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Abdullah ibn Raja al-Muzani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Any woman married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void, her marriage is void, her marriage is void. If he consummates with her, she is entitled to the dower for what he made lawful of her private part; and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian.”"
"234","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating, from Urwah, from Aisha, that she said: My uncle through nursing, Aflah ibn Abi al-Qu’ays, came seeking permission to visit me after the veil had been imposed, and I did not permit him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, I informed him, and he said: “He is your uncle, so permit him.”"
"235","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: And Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, with the addition that she said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, only the woman nursed me; the man did not nurse me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “May your right hand be dusty; he is your uncle, so permit him.”"
"236","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us — and it was among the best of what he narrated — from his father, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six or seven years old, and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old."
"237","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sa’id ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me while I was wearing hawf, and it was only that when he married me, modesty was cast upon me. Sufyan said: Al-hawf is garments of straps that the Bedouins dress their children in."
"238","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us — and I memorized it from him, and it was long, so I memorized from it this — he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah informed me, he said: I asked Aisha, saying: O mother, inform me about the illness of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he died. So she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became gravely ill in the illness in which he died, puffing as one who eats raisins puffs, and he used to go around to his wives. When he became heavy and his pain intensified, he sought their permission to stay with me, and they permitted him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me leaning on two men, one of whom was al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. Ubaydullah said: So I narrated it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: Did she not inform you of the other? I said: No. He said: The other was Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"239","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Isma’il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Sha’bi narrating, from Masruq, who said: I heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given his wives a choice, and they chose him; so was that a divorce?"
"240","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, from Ata, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until women were made lawful for him."
"241","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: They narrated to us from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his mother, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a wedding feast for one of his wives with barley. Al-Humaydi said: So we stopped Sufyan, and he said: I did not hear it."
"242","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Safwan al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “Charity (i.e. unpaid obligatory charity) never mixes with wealth except that it destroys it.” He said: It may be that charity has become due upon you from your wealth and you do not pay it, so the unlawful destroys the lawful."
"243","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Aisha saying: Sa’d ibn Abi Waqqas and Abd ibn Zam’ah disputed in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the son of the slave woman of Zam’ah. So Sa’d said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother Utbah advised me, saying: When you arrive at Makkah, look at the son of the slave woman of Zam’ah and take him, for he is my son. And Abd ibn Zam’ah said: O Messenger of Allah, he is my brother, the son of my father’s slave woman, and he was born on my father’s bed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a clear resemblance to Utbah, and said: “He is yours, O Abd ibn Zam’ah; the child belongs to the (marital) bed, and veil yourself from him, O Sawdah.” So it was said to Sufyan: Malik says: “And for the adulterer is the stone.” So Sufyan said: But we did not retain from al-Zuhri that he said it in this hadith."
"244","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me one day delighted and said: “O Aisha, have you not seen that Mujazziz al-Mudliji entered upon me and saw Zayd and Usamah, with a velvet cloth over them covering their heads while their feet were exposed, and said: These feet are part of one another.”"
"245","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Jurayj narrating it from al-Zuhri, and he said in it: “Have you not seen that Muhriz al-Mudliji...” So I said: O Abu al-Walid, it is only Mujazziz al-Mudliji. So he was corrected and retracted."
"246","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated to us, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aisha, who said: I wanted to buy Barirah and free her, but her masters stipulated upon me that I free her while the right of clientage would belong to them. So I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: “Buy her and free her, for clientage belongs only to the one who frees.” Then he addressed the people, saying: “What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions not in the Book of Allah? Whoever stipulates a condition not in the Book of Allah, it does not belong to him, even if he stipulates a hundred times; clientage belongs only to the one who frees.”"
"247","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that Hind bint Utbah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan is a miserly man, and I have nothing from him except what I take for my household. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Take what suffices you and your child according to what is customary.”"
"248","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My mother has died, and I think that had she spoken she would have given charity; so does she have reward if I give charity on her behalf? He said: “Yes.” Sufyan said: And the people retained from Hisham a phrase I did not retain, that he said: My mother’s soul was taken suddenly and she died. I did not retain it from Hisham; this phrase was only informed to me by Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Hisham."
"249","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the overwhelming of debt."
"250","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it. Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan did not hear it from al-Zuhri."
"251","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A’mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from an aunt of his, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Your children are among the best of your earnings, so eat from your earnings.”"
"252","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, who said: Abu Hurayrah sat beside the room of Aisha while she was praying, and began narrating, saying: Listen, O mistress of the room. When she finished her prayer, she said to me: O son of my sister, do you not wonder at this man and his narration? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would only speak words such that, had one counting them counted them, he would have enumerated them. Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan did not hear it from al-Zuhri."
"253","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aisha, that a group of Jews entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: “As-sam (death) be upon you, O Abu al-Qasim.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “And upon you.” So Aisha said: Rather upon you be death and the curse. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O Aisha, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves gentleness in every matter.” She said: I said: Did you not hear, O Messenger of Allah, what they said? They said: “As-sam be upon you.” So he said: “I have said: Upon you.” Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan would sometimes say in this hadith: “And upon you,” but when he was stopped upon it, he dropped the “waw” (saying only: “Upon you”)."
"254","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, that he heard Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrating, from Aisha, that he heard her saying: A man sought permission to visit the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Admit him; what an evil son of the tribe he is” — or he said: “Brother of the tribe.” When he entered, he spoke to him gently. When he left, I said: O Messenger of Allah, you said about him what you said, then you spoke gently to him? So he said: “O Aisha, the worst of people in rank before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is the one whom people abandon — or he said: whom people leave alone — out of fear of his obscenity.” Sufyan said: So I said to Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir: I see you always doubting in this hadith."
"255","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “No wealth ever benefited us as the wealth of Abu Bakr benefited us.” Al-Humaydi said: So it was said to Sufyan: Ma’mar narrates it from Sa’id. So he said: We heard it from al-Zuhri only from Urwah, from Aisha."
"256","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrating, that he heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I had screened myself with a curtain containing images. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, his face changed color, then he tore it down and said: “The most severely tormented of people before Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate Allah’s creation, Mighty and Majestic.” Sufyan said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim came to us, he narrated to us better than it and with concession, saying: My father informed me, that he heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived while I had covered a small storeroom of mine with a curtain of mine containing images. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw it, he removed it and said: “The most severely tormented of people before Allah on the Day of Resurrection are those who make likenesses of Allah’s creation, Mighty and Majestic.” Aisha said: So we cut from it a cushion or two cushions."
"257","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd Rabbih ibn Sa’id narrated to us, from Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Aisha, that when a person complained of something, or had an ulcer or a wound, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say with his finger like this — and Abu Bakr placed his forefinger on the ground, then raised it: “In the Name of Allah; the dust of our land with the saliva of some of us; our sick is healed by the permission of our Lord.”"
"258","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, that he heard Sa’d ibn Ibrahim narrating, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There were among the nations before you inspired men (muhaddathun); if there is one in this nation, it is Umar ibn al-Khattab.”"
"259","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha... He said: Ya’qub ibn Zayd al-Taymi narrated to us, from Aisha, who said: Some Abyssinians were playing with their spears, and I would watch from between the ear and the shoulder of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until I was the one who turned away. Ya’qub ibn Zayd added in his hadith: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is none of them except that a devil has seized his garment, saying: Look; but when Umar came, the devils dispersed.” She said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Play, O Banu Arfidah, so that the Jews and Christians know that there is latitude in our religion.” Aisha said: I did not retain from their words except this phrase: “Abu al-Qasim is good, Abu al-Qasim is good.”"
"260","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine melon with fresh dates and eat them."
"261","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, who said: al-Harith ibn Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How does revelation come to you? So he said: “It comes to me sometimes like the ringing of a bell, then it leaves me after I have comprehended from it, and it is the hardest upon me; and it comes to me sometimes in the form of a young man, and he conveys it to me, and I comprehend it, and that is the easiest upon me.”"
"262","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ma’mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, who said: The most beloved drink to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the sweet cold drink."
"263","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: al-Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu’tamir, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aisha, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) avenging a wrong done to him, so long as the sanctities of Allah were not violated; but when something of the sanctities of Allah was violated, he was the angriest of them in that regard. And he was never given a choice between two matters except that he chose the easier of them, so long as it was not sinful."
"264","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained such-and-such a time imagining that he visited his wives while he did not visit them. She said: So one day he said: “O Aisha, have you known that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given me a ruling concerning a matter about which I sought His ruling? Two men came to me; one of them sat at my feet and the other at my head. The one at my feet said to the one at my head: What is the matter with the man? He said: He is bewitched (matbub). He said: And who bewitched him? He said: Labid ibn al-A’sam. He said: And in what? He said: In the sheath of a male palm spathe, in a comb and combings, beneath a stone in the well of Dharwan.” She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to it and said: “This is the well I was shown; it is as though the heads of its palm trees are the heads of devils, and its water as though the infusion of henna.” She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded concerning it, and it was taken out. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you not...? Sufyan said: Meaning: publicize it (seek a charm/remedy openly). So he said: “By Allah, He has healed me; as for me, I dislike stirring up evil therefrom against the people.” She said: And Labid ibn al-A’sam was a man of Banu Zurayq, an ally of the Jews. Sufyan said: Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj had narrated it to us first before we met Hisham, saying: Some of the family of Urwah narrated to me; then when Hisham arrived, he narrated it to us."
"265","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, who said: I used to play with these dolls, and slave girls would come to me playing with me with them; when they saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they withdrew, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send them to me."
"266","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that she said: I raced the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I outran him; then when I became heavy with flesh, he raced me and outran me. So he said: “O Aisha, this is for that.”"
"267","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Let none of you say: I am khabith al-nafs (wicked in soul); rather let him say: I am laqis al-nafs (uneasy in soul).”"
"268","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, who said: Aisha said to me: O son of my sister, your two fathers were indeed among those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after injury befell them... Abu Bakr and al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam."
"269","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Jami’ ibn Abi Rashid narrated to us, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, from a woman, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When evil appears openly in the land, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sends down His punishment upon the people of the land.” She said: So I said: Shall we perish while among us are people obedient to Allah? He said: “Yes; then you will return to the mercy of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.”"
"270","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his paternal aunt Aisha bint Talhah, from her maternal aunt Aisha, Mother of the Believers, who said: A boy of the children of the Ansar was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to pray over him, so I said: Glad tidings for him; a sparrow of the sparrows of Paradise; he never did any evil, nor did sin overtake him. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Or other than that, O Aisha! Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created Paradise and created people for it, creating them while they were in the loins of their fathers; and He created Hell and created people for it, creating them while they were in the loins of their fathers.”"
"271","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za’idah, from Abbas ibn Dharih, from al-Sha’bi, who said: Mu’awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan wrote to Aisha: Write to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So she wrote to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “Whoever acts in disobedience to Allah, his praiser among the people will turn into a blamer.”"
"272","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma’il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha’bi, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never sent an expedition in which Zayd ibn Harithah was present except that he appointed him commander over them."
"273","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma’il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Sahlah, from Aisha, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: “I wish I had with me a man of my Companions.” So I said: Shall we not call Abu Bakr for you? He said: “No.” Then he said: “I wish I had with me a man of my Companions.” So I said: Shall we not call Umar for you? He said: “No.” Then he said: “I wish I had with me a man of my Companions.” So I said: Shall we not call your cousin Ali ibn Abi Talib for you? He said: “No.” Then he said: “I wish I had with me a man of my Companions.” So I said: Shall we not call Uthman for you? He fell silent. She said: So I ordered him to be called, and when he came to him, he was alone with him; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept speaking to him while Uthman’s face kept changing color. Sufyan said: And they narrated to me from Ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Abu Sahlah, that Aisha said in this hadith: I retained nothing of his words except that he said: “If they ask you to divest yourself of a shirt with which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has clothed you, do not do so.”"
"274","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa’id, from Isma’il ibn Abi Hakim, who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not punish the general public for the deeds of the elite; but when sins appear openly and are not changed, the general and the elite are both seized."
"275","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, from al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, from his father, from Aisha, who said: When we were given rain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: “O Allah, a flowing beneficial (rain).” Sufyan said: Thus I memorized it: “sayban”; but what they memorized is more precise: “sayyiban”."
"276","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: I asked Aisha about the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so she said: Are you asking about the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left neither yellow (gold) nor white (silver), neither sheep nor camel, neither male nor female slave, neither gold nor silver."
"277","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, who said: It was mentioned to Aisha that a woman wears sandals, so she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed masculine women."
"278","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan and Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The most hated of men to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the fiercely contentious adversary.”"
"279","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha’bi, from Masruq, from Aisha, that she said: O Messenger of Allah: {On the Day the earth will be changed to other than the earth} — where will the people be that Day? He said: “Upon the Bridge (as-Sirat), O daughter of as-Siddiq.”"
"280","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa’id ibn Wahb, from Aisha, that she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying, Mighty and Majestic: {And those who give what they give while their hearts are fearful} — are they those who commit adultery, steal, and drink wine? He said: “No, O daughter of as-Siddiq; rather they are those who pray, fast, and give charity.”"
"281","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A’mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa’il, from Masruq, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When a woman spends from her husband’s house without causing harm, he has (reward) for what he earned, she has (reward) for what she spent, and the storekeeper has the like of that.”"
"282","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Sa’id, from al-Sha’bi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aisha, that she said: I saw you, O Messenger of Allah, placing your hand upon the withers of a horse while you were standing speaking to Dihyah al-Kalbi. So he said: “And did you see him?” She said: Yes. He said: “That was Gabriel, and he conveys greetings of peace to you.” She said: Upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah; may Allah reward him well as a visitor and as a guest; what an excellent companion and what an excellent guest."
"283","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from his father, from Aisha, who said: Sahlah bint Suhayl came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I see dislike in the face of Abu Hudhayfah due to Salim entering upon me, so he said: “Nurse him.” So she said: How can I nurse him when he is a grown man? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: “I already know that he is a grown man.” She said: So she nursed him, then she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have not seen in the face of Abu Hudhayfah anything I dislike since I nursed him. Abd al-Rahman said: And he had been present at Badr."
"284","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman informed me, that she heard Aisha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Cutting (the hand) is for a quarter dinar and above.”"
"285","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: And four narrated it to us from Amrah, from Aisha, without raising it (to the Prophet): Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, Ruzayq ibn Hakim al-Ayli, Yahya ibn Sa’id, and Abd Rabbih ibn Sa’id; and al-Zuhri was the most retentive of them all, except that in the hadith of Yahya there is what indicates raising it, which I have not forgotten though it has been long upon me: “Cutting (the hand) is for a quarter dinar and above.”"
"286","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Every drink that intoxicates is unlawful.” So it was said to Sufyan: Malik and others mention al-bit’ (a Yemeni honey drink). So he said: Ibn Shihab did not tell us al-bit’; Ibn Shihab told us only as I told you."
"287","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the recitation of Abu Musa and said: “This man has been given of the melodious voices of the family of Dawud.” And Sufyan would sometimes doubt in it, saying: From Amrah or Urwah, not mentioning the report in it; then he became firm upon Urwah, mentioning the report in it more than once and abandoning the doubt."
"288","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aisha, that gold had come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he woke in the night (restless), while it was more than seven and less than nine; he did not reach morning until he had distributed it, then he said: “What would Muhammad think of his Lord, had he died while this was with him?” Sufyan said: I think it was charity that had come to him, or the right of a person which he feared would be lost."
"289","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Wa’il ibn Dawud, from his son Bakr ibn Wa’il, from al-Zuhri, from Sa’id ibn al-Musayyib, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: “O Aisha, if you have committed a sin, seek Allah’s forgiveness; for when a servant commits a sin then repents and seeks Allah’s forgiveness, Mighty and Majestic, Allah forgives him.” Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan would sometimes say: “If you have committed a sin, seek Allah’s forgiveness; for repentance is remorse and seeking forgiveness...” And most of the time he said it upon the first wording."
"290","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Amrah, from Aisha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I entered Paradise and heard recitation therein, so I said: Who is this? So they said: Harithah ibn al-Nu’man; such is righteousness, such is righteousness.” So it was said to Sufyan: Is it from Amrah? He said: Yes, no doubt in it; thus al-Zuhri said."
"291","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Safwan ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan al-Jumahi narrated to us, he said: I heard my grandfather Abdullah ibn Safwan, during the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr, in al-Hijr, saying: I heard Hafsah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “An army will surely intend this House, raiding it, until when they are at a desert plain of the land, their middle will be swallowed up; their first will call out to their last, and none of them will escape except the lone survivor who informs about them.” So a man said to my grandfather: I bear witness that you have not lied about Hafsah, and that Hafsah did not lie about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sufyan said: And Umayr ibn Qays used to narrate it from Umayyah, and I would not dare to ask him about it; he used to sit with Khalid ibn Muhammad and Abdullah ibn Shaybah, who were among the greatest of Quraysh in that day, and they used to sit in Suq al-Layl, while they were then at the gate of the mosque. Umayyah sought my help to look for Khalid ibn Muhammad for him, and I do not know whether I found him for him or not; when he sought my help, I dared upon him and asked him, and he narrated it to me."
"292","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Hafsah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take something from the face (kiss) of one of his wives while he was fasting."
"293","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Countless of the companions of Nafi’ narrated to us, from Nafi’, from Ibn Umar, who said: Hafsah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when dawn became clear to him, would pray two rak’ahs."
"294","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Nabhan, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, informed me, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When one of you has a mukatab (contracted slave) and he has what he can pay, she should veil herself from him.” Sufyan said: My retention from al-Zuhri ended here; afterwards Ma’mar informed me from al-Zuhri, from Nabhan, who said: I used to lead Umm Salamah’s mule, and she said to me: O Nabhan, how much remains upon you of your contract? So I said: A thousand dirhams. He said: So she said: Do you have what you can pay? I said: Yes. She said: Then pay it to so-and-so — a brother of hers or a nephew — and she cast the veil, saying: Peace be upon you, O Nabhan; this is the last you shall see of me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When one of you has a mukatab and he has what he can pay, she should veil herself from him.” So I said: I do not have what I can pay, nor am I one to pay."
"295","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ammar al-Duhni narrated to us — we did not find it with anyone besides him — that he heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and the legs of my pulpit are fixed in Paradise.”"
"296","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Umm Salamah, that she said: When Abu Salamah died, I said: A stranger in a strange land; I shall surely weep over him a weeping that will be spoken of. She said: So I prepared to weep, and a woman from Upper Egypt came wanting to help me weep, so when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw her, he met her saying: “Do you wish to bring Satan into a house from which Allah has expelled him? Do you wish to bring Satan into a house from which Allah has expelled him?” Umm Salamah said: So I abandoned weeping and did not weep."
"297","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar and Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Umm Salamah. And Ma’mar narrated it to us from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one night: “Glory be to Allah! What trials have befallen, and what treasures have been opened! Wake the occupants of the rooms; for many a clothed one in this world will be naked on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"298","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, that he heard Sa’id ibn al-Musayyib narrating, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When the ten (days of Dhul-Hijjah) enter and one of you intends to sacrifice, let him not touch any of his hair or skin.” Abu Bakr said: It was said to Sufyan: Some of them do not raise it (to the Prophet). He said: But I raise it."
"299","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Rafi’, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, that Umm Salamah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I am a woman who braids the hair of my head tightly; should I undo it for the bath of janabah? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “No; it suffices you to pour over your head three handfuls of water, then pour water over yourself and you will be purified.” Or he said: “Then you will have been purified.”"
"300","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Labid narrated to us — and he was among the worshippers of the people of Madinah, though he held the doctrine of qadar — that he heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan arrived at Madinah, and while he was upon the pulpit, he said to Kathir ibn al-Salt: Go to Aisha, Mother of the Believers, and ask her about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the two rak’ahs after Asr. Abu Salamah said: So I went with him, and Abdullah ibn Abbas sent Abdullah ibn al-Harith with us, saying: Go and hear what the Mother of the Believers says. Abu Salamah said: So he came to her and asked her, and she said: I have no knowledge, but go to Umm Salamah and ask her. So I went with him to Umm Salamah and he asked her, and Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me one day after Asr and prayed two rak’ahs with me, though I had never seen him praying them. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, you have prayed a prayer I had never seen you praying. He said: “I used to pray two rak’ahs after Zuhr, and a delegation of Banu Tamim — or charity — came to me and distracted me from them, so these are those two rak’ahs.”"
"301","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from her mother Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I am only a human being; you dispute before me, and perhaps some of you is more eloquent in his plea than others. So whomever I judge for something of his brother’s right, let him not take it; for I am only cutting for him thereby a piece of the Fire.”"
"302","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from her mother Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while with me was an effeminate man (mukhannath); I heard him saying to Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah: O Abdullah, if Allah grants you victory over al-Ta’if tomorrow, take to yourself the daughter of Ghaylan, for she comes forward with four and turns back with eight. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “These shall not enter upon you.” Sufyan said: And Ibn Jurayj said: His name was Hit."
"303","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from her mother Umm Salamah, that Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, Allah is not shy of the truth; is ghusl obligatory upon a woman when she has a wet dream? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When one of you sees water, let her wash.” So Umm Salamah said: And does a woman have a wet dream? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “May your right hand be dusty; then from what comes the resemblance?”"
"304","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Sa’id al-Thawri narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Aisha, from a freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say after Fajr: “O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, wholesome provision, and accepted deeds.”"
"305","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Salamah, a man of the descendants of Umm Salamah, informed me, that al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam disputed with a man before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged for al-Zubayr. So the man said: He only judged for him because he is the son of his paternal aunt. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what arises between them, then find in themselves no discomfort from what you have decreed, and submit in full submission.}"
"306","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Salamah, a man of the descendants of Umm Salamah, informed me, from Umm Salamah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not hear Allah, Mighty and Majestic, mentioning women in emigration with anything. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: {So their Lord responded to them: I shall not waste the deed of any doer among you, male or female} — the verse."
"307","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, that she said: Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh suffered prolonged non-menstrual bleeding (istihadah), so she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: “It is not menstruation; rather it is a vein.” And he commanded her to leave prayer for the duration of her menstrual periods, or the duration of her menstruation, then wash; and if the blood overcomes her, she should pad herself with a cloth and pray."
"308","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha’bi, from Umm Salamah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left his house, he would say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from slipping or straying, wronging or being wronged, acting ignorantly or being treated ignorantly.”"
"309","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa’id narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Nafi’, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from her mother Umm Salamah, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter’s husband has died, and she complains of her eye; may she apply kohl? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Each of you would throw the dung upon the head of the year; now it is only four months and ten days.” Yahya said: So I said to Humayd ibn Nafi’: What is his saying: “Each of you would throw the dung upon the head of the year”? So he said: In the pre-Islamic ignorance, a woman would wear the shabbiest of her clothes, of her lowliest garments, then enter the lowliest of her houses. When the head of the year arrived, she would take a dung pellet and throw it over another’s back — and perhaps Abu Bakr said: backwards — saying: I have become lawful (to remarry)."
"310","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Shawwal informed me, from Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): we would depart early in darkness from Muzdalifah to Mina. Sufyan said: And Salim ibn Shawwal is a man of the people of Makkah; we have heard no one narrating from him except Amr ibn Dinar this hadith."
"311","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Nafi’ informed me, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, who said: When the news of Abu Sufyan’s death came from Syria, Umm Habibah called for yellow perfume on the third day, wiped her cheeks and forearms with it, and said: I was in no need of this, were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three (days), except over a husband, for she mourns over him for four months and ten days.” So it was said to Sufyan: Malik says in it: From Humayd ibn Nafi’, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, and from Safiyyah and Umm Habibah. So Sufyan said: Ayyub ibn Musa told us only Umm Habibah."
"312","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: O Messenger of Allah, do you have any interest in Durrah bint Abi Sufyan? He said: “What would I do?” She said: I said: You marry her. He said: “And do you love that?” I said: I am not alone with you (i.e. I do not have you to myself exclusively), and the one I most love to share me in you is my sister. He said: “She is not lawful for me.” I said: It has reached me that you are betrothing Zaynab bint Abi Salamah. So he said: “The daughter of Umm Salamah?” I said: Yes. He said: “By Allah, even if she were not my stepdaughter in my care, she would not be lawful for me; Thuwaybah nursed me and her father, so do not present your daughters or your sisters to me.”"
"313","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us — we need no one else in it — he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Habibah bint Umm Habibah, from her mother Umm Habibah, from Zaynab bint Jahsh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke from sleep with his face red, saying: “There is no deity but Allah, there is no deity but Allah! Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near; today there has been opened of the barrier of Ya’juj and Ma’juj the like of this.” And Sufyan made a circle with ten (his fingers). I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perish while among us are the righteous? He said: “Yes, when wickedness increases.” Sufyan said: I retain in this hadith four women from al-Zuhri, all of whom saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): two of his wives, Umm Habibah and Zaynab bint Jahsh, and two of his stepdaughters, Zaynab bint Umm Salamah and Habibah bint Umm Habibah, whose father Ubaydullah ibn Jahsh died in the land of Abyssinia."
"314","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Sha’tha, Jabir ibn Zayd, informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas saying: Maymunah informed me that she used to wash with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a single vessel. Then Sufyan said: This chain used to please Shu’bah: “I heard; he informed me; I heard; he informed me” — as though he desired its continuity."
"315","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Manbudh al-Makki narrated to us, from his mother, who said: We were with Maymunah when Ibn Abbas entered upon her, so she said: O my son, why do I see you disheveled in your head? He said: My hairdresser Umm Ammar is menstruating. So she said: O my son, what has menstruation to do with the hands? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would place his head in the lap of one of us while she was menstruating, then recite the Qur’an; and one of us would stand to him with his khumrah (small prayer mat), spread it for him while she was menstruating, and he would pray upon it. O my son, what has menstruation to do with the hand?"
"316","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad — or Yazid ibn al-Asamm, Sufyan being the one who doubts — from Maymunah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon the khumrah (small prayer mat)."
"317","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, that he heard Ibn Abbas narrating, from Maymunah, that a mouse fell into clarified butter and died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it and said: “Throw it away with what is around it, and eat it.” Abu Bakr said: So it was said to Sufyan: Ma’mar narrates it from al-Zuhri, from Sa’id, from Abu Hurayrah. Sufyan said: I heard al-Zuhri narrating it only from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and I heard it from him many times."
"318","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had, from Maymunah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a woolen garment (mirt), part of which was upon him and part upon me, while I was menstruating."
"319","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Sulayman, Abdullah ibn Abdullah, nephew of Yazid ibn al-Asamm — the elder of the two — narrated to us, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, that she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated, had a lamb wished to pass beneath him, it could have passed, so widely did he spread his arms."
"320","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep belonging to a freed slave woman of Maymunah, which she had been given from charity, and said: “What is upon the owners of this (sheep), had they taken its hide, tanned it, and benefited from it?” So they said: O Messenger of Allah, it is carrion. So he said: “Only eating it is unlawful.” So it was said to Sufyan: Ma’mar does not say in it: “So they tan it,” and says: al-Zuhri used to deny tanning. So Sufyan said: But I retained it; we only wanted from it this phrase which none besides him stated: “Only eating it is unlawful.” And Sufyan would sometimes not mention Maymunah in it; when he was stopped upon it, he said in it: Maymunah."
"321","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-A’mash narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Maymunah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed from janabah: he washed his private part with his hand, then rubbed it against the wall, then washed it, then performed ablution as for prayer; when he finished his washing, he washed his feet."
"322","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq informed me, that he heard Juwayriyah bint al-Harith saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me one day and said: “Is there any food?” So I said: No, except a bone given to a freed slave woman of ours from charity. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place (it is no longer charity).” Abu Bakr said: Meaning: It is not charity now."
"323","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, that he heard his father saying: Asma bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed me, who said: My mother came to me, desirous (of gifts/visiting), in the treaty period of Quraysh, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Shall I maintain ties with her? He said: “Yes.” Sufyan said: And concerning it was revealed: {Allah does not forbid you concerning those who did not fight you} — the verse."
"324","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, that he heard his wife Fatimah bint al-Mundhir narrating, from her grandmother Asma, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “One who pretends to be satiated with what he has not been given is like the wearer of two garments of falsehood.”"
"325","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, that he heard his wife Fatimah bint al-Mundhir narrating, that she heard Asma bint Abi Bakr saying: A woman asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about menstrual blood touching a garment, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Scrape it, then rub it with water, then sprinkle it with water, and pray in it.”"
"326","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, that he heard Fatimah bint al-Mundhir saying: I heard Asma saying: A woman asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, my daughter was struck with measles, so her hair fell out in tufts, and I have married her off; may I add (extensions) to it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah has cursed the woman who adds hair and the woman to whom it is added.”"
"327","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Fatimah bint al-Mundhir, from her grandmother Asma, who said: We slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate it."
"328","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Tadrus, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, who said: When {Perish the hands of Abu Lahab} was revealed, al-Awra Umm Jamil bint Harb came forth wailing, with a stone (fihr) in her hand, saying: “Mudhammam (the dispraised one) we have renounced, his religion we have detested, and his command we have disobeyed.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque, having recited Qur’an, with Abu Bakr beside him. When Abu Bakr saw her, he said: O Messenger of Allah, she has come and I fear she will see you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “She will not see me.” And he recited Qur’an by which he sought protection, as he said, and recited: {And when you recite the Qur’an, We place between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter a concealed veil.} So she came forth until she stood over Abu Bakr, without seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Abu Bakr, I have been informed that your companion has lampooned me. So he said: No, by the Lord of this House, he has not lampooned you. He said: So she turned away saying: Quraysh know that I am the daughter of their chief. Al-Walid said in his hadith — or another said: So Umm Jamil stumbled while circumambulating the House in her woolen wrap, saying: Perish Mudhammam. So Umm Hakim bint Abd al-Muttalib said: I am chaste, so I am not reviled; and sound in judgment, so I am not taught; both of us are of the cousins’ line; Quraysh thereafter know best."
"329","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Tadrus, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that they said to her: What is the worst you saw the polytheists do to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So she said: The polytheists sat in the mosque discussing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what he says concerning their gods. While they were thus, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered; so they rose against him. When they asked about anything, he would tell them the truth. So they said: Do you not say such-and-such? So he said: “Yes.” So they seized him all together. The cry for help reached Abu Bakr; it was said to him: Reach your companion. So he came out from us, and he had braids of hair; he entered the mosque saying: Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah, when he has come to you with clear proofs from your Lord? He said: So they left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alone and turned upon Abu Bakr. So Abu Bakr returned to us, and he would not touch anything of his braids except that it came away with him, while he was saying: Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"330","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: “O Asma, do not withhold (in giving), lest it be withheld from you.”"
"331","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muhayyah narrated to us, from his father, that he said: When al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf killed Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, al-Hajjaj entered upon Asma bint Abi Bakr and said to her: O mother, the Commander of the Believers has enjoined me concerning you; do you have any need? She said: I have no need, nor am I a mother to you; rather I am the mother of the one crucified atop the mountain pass. But wait, I shall narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “There will emerge from Thaqif a liar and a destroyer.” As for the liar, we have seen him — meaning al-Mukhtar — and as for the destroyer, it is you. So al-Hajjaj said: A destroyer of hypocrites."
"332","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: The brother of al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: One who heard Asma bint Abi Bakr saying informed me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O assembly of believing women, let no woman of you raise her head before the imam raises his head” — due to the tightness of the men’s garments."
"333","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: They informed me from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah ibn Abi Mu’ayt, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: “The best charity is upon the hostile relative.” Sufyan said: And I did not hear it from al-Zuhri. Abu Bakr said: Al-kashih means: the enemy."
"334","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any sin upon me if I lie to my wife? He said: No, for Allah does not love lying. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I seek to reconcile with her and please her. He said: There is no sin upon you."
"335","The narration of Asma bint Umays. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Urwa ibn Amir, from Ubayd ibn Rifaa, from Asma bint Umays, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, the sons of Jafar are struck by the evil eye; shall I seek ruqya for them? He said: Yes, for if anything were to outstrip the decree, the evil eye would outstrip it."
"336","Narrations of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Murra the freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani, who said: On the day of the Conquest, two of my brothers-in-law came to me and I granted them protection, then Ali came wanting to kill them, so I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in his tent at al-Abtah in upper Mecca but I did not find him, and I found Fatima, who was harsher toward me than Ali, and she said: Do you shelter the disbelievers and grant them protection, and do this and that? Soon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with traces of dust on his face, and he said: O Fatima, pour out water for me to wash with. She poured washing water for him in a bowl, and it was as if I could still see traces of dough in it, then she screened him with a garment, and he washed himself, then he prayed eight rakahs in a single garment with its two ends crossed in opposite directions, which I had never seen him pray before or after. When he finished, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have granted protection to two of my brothers-in-law, but my brother Ali wants to kill them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has no right to do that; we have granted protection to whomever you granted protection, and we have given safety to whomever you gave safety."
"337","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrating, from Umm Hani, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the Conquest pray eight rakahs in a single garment with its two ends crossed in opposite directions."
"338","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya said: Abdullah ibn al-Harith said, and he did not say to us in it that he heard it directly, he said: I asked about the Duha prayer during the rule of Uthman when the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were numerous, and I did not find anyone who affirmed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me except Umm Hani, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray it once, on the day of the Conquest, eight rakahs in a single garment with its two ends crossed in opposite directions."
"339","Abdullah ibn al-Harith said: I mentioned it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: I used to pass by this verse, They glorify Him in the evening and at sunrise, and I would say: What prayer is the sunrise prayer? So this is the sunrise prayer."
"340","Narrations of Khawla bint Hakim, wife of Uthman ibn Mazun. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysara narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Suwayd, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, who said: The righteous woman Khawla bint Hakim, wife of Uthman ibn Mazun, claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out holding one of his daughter's two sons close to him, saying: By Allah, they make you ignorant and cowardly and miserly, yet they are of the fragrance of Allah, and the last footstep the Lord of the worlds trod was at Wajj."
"341","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Insan narrated to me, meaning Ibn Insan, a clan of the Arabs, from Abdullah ibn Abd Rabbihi ibn al-Hakam ibn Uthman ibn Bishr, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Kab, that he heard him say: Wajj is sacred; from it the Lord ascended to the heaven on the day He completed the creation of the earth. Al-Humaydi said: Wajj is at Taif."
"342","Narrations of Umm Khalid bint Khalid ibn al-As. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqba narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Khalid bint Khalid say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking refuge from the punishment of the grave. Musa said: And I did not hear of anyone besides her who heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"343","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Said al-Saidi narrated to us, from his father, from Umm Khalid bint Khalid, who said: I came from the land of Abyssinia when I was a young girl, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a patterned woolen garment that had marks on it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to rub the marks with his hand, saying: Sanah, sanah. Abu Bakr said: Meaning good, good."
"344","Narrations of Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from his mother Umm al-Fadl, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib, By those sent forth in succession. It was said to Sufyan: But they say it was Tammam ibn Abbas. He said: I never heard al-Zuhri mention Tammam at all; he only said to us: from Ibn Abbas, from his mother."
"345","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salim Abu al-Nadr narrated to us that he heard Umayr, the freedman of Umm al-Fadl, narrating from Umm al-Fadl, who said: The people doubted whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting on the day of Arafa, so she sent him a vessel containing milk, and he drank. Sufyan would sometimes word this narration: The people doubt whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is fasting on the day of Arafa, so Umm al-Fadl sent to him, and when he was pressed on it, he would say: It is from Umm al-Fadl."
"346","Narrations of Umm Ayyub. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: My father informed me that Umm Ayyub al-Ansariyya informed him, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with us, and we prepared food for him containing some of these greens, and he disliked it, and he said to his Companions: Eat, for I am not like any one of you; I dislike troubling my companion. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about what is narrated from you, that the angels are troubled by whatever the children of Adam are troubled by? He said: True."
"347","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: I stayed with Umm Ayyub al-Ansariyya, and she informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was revealed in seven modes; whichever of them you recite, you are correct."
"348","Narrations of Umayma bint Ruqayqa, kinswoman of Khadija. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Umayma bint Ruqayqa saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with a group of women, and he said: In what you are able and capable of. I said: Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves; O Messenger of Allah, accept our pledge. He said: I do not shake hands with women; my word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman. Abu Bakr said: It was said to Sufyan: But they say in it: Umayma bint Ruqayqa, kinswoman of Khadija. Sufyan said: She is the kinswoman of Khadija, but Ibn al-Munkadir did not say it to us."
"349","Narrations of al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn sent me to al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra to ask her about the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), for he used to perform ablution at her house, so I went to her and she brought out to me a vessel holding a mudd or a mudd and a quarter by the mudd of Ibn Hisham, and she said: With this I used to bring out water for the ablution of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would begin by washing his hands three times before putting them into the vessel, then rinse his mouth and nose three times each, and wash his face three times, then wash his hands three times each, then wipe his head front to back, and wash his feet three times each. She said: A cousin of yours came to me and asked me about it, and I informed him, and he said: I know of nothing in the Book of Allah except two washings and two wipings, meaning Ibn Abbas. Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan described the wiping for us, placing his hands on his temples, then wiping with them to his forehead, then lifting them and placing them on his temples from the middle of his head, then wiping to his nape. Sufyan said: And Ibn Ajlan had narrated it to us first from Ibn Aqil from al-Rubayyi, adding in the wiping: then he wiped from his temples over his cheeks until reaching the tip of his beard, but when we asked Ibn Aqil about it, he did not describe the cheeks to us in the wiping, and there was something in his memory, so I disliked prompting him."
"350","Narrations of Umm Qays bint Mihsan al-Asadiyya of Asad Khuzayma. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba informed me that he heard Umm Qays bint Mihsan al-Asadiyya saying: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of mine who had not yet eaten food, and he urinated on him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water and sprinkled it over it."
"351","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me that he heard Umm Qays bint Mihsan saying: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of mine, and I had treated his throat ailment with a finger-press, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you torture your children with this pressing? Use this Indian aloeswood, for it contains seven cures: it is inhaled for throat ailments and given through the side of the mouth for pleurisy. Al-Zuhri said: Ubaydullah explained two to us and did not explain five to us. Al-Humaydi said: Indian aloeswood is costus."
"352","Narrations of Umm Kurz al-Khuzaiyya. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, he said: My father informed me that he heard Siba ibn Thabit narrating that he heard Umm Kurz al-Kabiyya saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For a boy two sheep, and for a girl one sheep; it does not matter to you whether they are male or female."
"353","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Abi Rabah informed me that Habiba bint Maysara al-Fihriyya, his freedwoman, informed him that she heard Umm Kurz al-Khuzaiyya saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In the aqiqa, for a boy two equivalent sheep, and for a girl one sheep."
"354","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, he said: My father informed me that he heard Siba ibn Thabit saying: I heard Umm Kurz al-Kabiyya saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Hudaybiyya seeking some of the meat of the sacrificial animals, and I heard him saying: Leave the birds upon their roosts."
"355","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, he said: My father informed me that he heard Siba ibn Thabit narrating that he heard Umm Kurz saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Prophethood has gone, and only the good tidings remain. Sufyan used to narrate this from Ubaydullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as mursal for a time, then he narrated it from his father, from Siba, from Umm Kurz, mentioning that he used to omit its chain until he established it later."
"356","Narrations of Umm Haram. Abu Tahir Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Jafar ibn Zayd al-Muaddib informed us, reading to him while I listened, in the year 427, and he acknowledged it, he said: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sawwaf narrated to us: Bishr narrated to us, he said: Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Maymun al-Juhani al-Ramli narrated to us, from Yala ibn Shaddad Abu Thabit, from Umm Haram, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the sea expedition: For the seasick one is the reward of a martyr, and for the drowned one the reward of two martyrs. She said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah the Exalted that He make me among them. He said: O Allah, make her among them. So she took part in the sea expedition, and when she came out she mounted her animal, fell, and died."
"357","Narration of Umm Sharik. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr ibn Shayba al-Hajabi narrated to me that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyib saying: Umm Sharik informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded her to kill geckos."
"358","Narration of Buqayra. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us that he heard Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi narrating, from Buqayra, wife of al-Qaqa ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying upon the pulpit: O people, when you hear of an army swallowed up nearby, then the Hour has cast its shadow."
"359","Narrations of Busra bint Safwan. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, he said: My father and Urwa ibn al-Zubayr discussed what requires ablution, and Urwa mentioned touching the private part, so my father said: This is something I have never heard of. Urwa said: Rather, Marwan ibn al-Hakam informed me that he heard Busra bint Safwan saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution. I said to Marwan: I would like you to send to her, so he sent a man to her while I was present, or he said: a guard, and the messenger returned from her saying that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"360","Narrations of Khawla bint Qays, wife of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah informed me, from Ubayd Sanuta, he said: I heard Khawla bint Qays, wife of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conversing with Hamza about the world, saying: The world is sweet and green; whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it, but many a one who plunges into the wealth of Allah and His Messenger will have the Fire on the day he meets Him. And Sufyan would sometimes say: on the Day of Resurrection."
"361","Narrations of Kabsha. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amra informed me, from his grandmother Kabsha, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me one day and drank from the mouth of a hanging waterskin while standing. She said: So I cut off the mouth of the waterskin. And Sufyan would sometimes say: Kabsha or Kubaysha, and most often he would say: Kubaysha."
"362","Narrations of the paternal aunt of Husayn ibn Mihsan. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Bushayr ibn Yasar informed me, from Husayn ibn Mihsan, from an aunt of his, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for some need, and he said: O woman, do you have a husband? I said: Yes. He said: Where do you stand with him? She said: I said: I do not fall short except in what I am unable to do. He said: Where do you stand with him, for he is your Paradise and your Fire."
"363","Narrations of Umm Mabad. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Mabad ibn Kab informed me, from his mother, who had prayed toward both qiblas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding mixed brews of dates and raisins to be steeped together. He said: Steep each one of them separately."
"364","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Kab, from his uncle or from his mother, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn, O people, for simplicity is part of faith."
"365","Narrations of Umm Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us that he heard Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas narrating from his mother, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning the jamra from the bottom of the valley while he was upon a mule, saying: O people, calmness is upon you; let none of you kill one another, and use pebbles like those used for slinging."
"366","Narration of Umm Husayn. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, narrating from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umm al-Husayn, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon while wrapped in a cloak, with his upper arm muscle trembling."
"367","Narrations of Umm Atiyya al-Ansariyya. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Abi Tamima al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyya, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us while we were washing his daughter, and he said: Wash her three times or five times or more than that if you see fit, with water and lote leaves, and put camphor or something of camphor in the last wash, and when you finish, inform me. When we finished, we informed him, and he gave us his waist-wrapper, saying: Wrap her in it."
"368","Sufyan said: And Ayyub narrated it to us, from Hafsa bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyya, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, adding in it, she said: And we made her head into three braids."
"369","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Hafsa bint Sirin, from a woman, from her sister, whose husband had taken part with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in more than ten expeditions, she being with him in six of them, she said: We used to treat the wounded and care for the sick. She said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there any sin upon one of us if she has no outer cloak and does not attend the Eid? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her sister clothe her with her cloak, and let her attend the Eid and the supplication of the Muslims."
"370","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Hafsa, who said: We asked Umm Atiyya: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: Yes, by my father, and whenever she narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she would say: By my father, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Bring out the unmarried maidens and those in seclusion; let them attend the Eid and the supplication of the Muslims, and let the menstruating women keep away from the prayer place of the Muslims."
"371","Narrations of Fatima bint Qays al-Fihriyya. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Said al-Hamdani narrated to us, from al-Shabi, who said: Fatima bint Qays came to Kufa to her brother al-Dahhak ibn Qays, who was its governor, and we went to her and asked her, and she said: I was with Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn al-Mughira, and he divorced me with an irrevocable divorce and left for Yemen, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, seeking maintenance, and he gestured with his sleeve like this, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) veiling himself from the woman, while Abu Bakr raised his sleeve above his head: Listen to me, O daughter of the family of Qays; lodging and maintenance are for the woman only when her husband retains the right of return over her, but if he has no right of return over her, then she has neither lodging nor maintenance. Then he said to me: Observe your waiting period at the house of Umm Sharik bint Abi al-Akr. Then he said: She is a woman at whose house people converse; observe your waiting period at the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, for he is a man deprived of sight, so you may lay aside your garments and he will not see you."
"372","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Shabi, who said: Fatima bint Qays al-Fihriyya came to Kufa to her brother al-Dahhak ibn Qays, who had been appointed over it, and we went to her asking her, and she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at midday, saying: I have not addressed you out of desire or fear, but because of a narration Tamim al-Dari narrated to me, whose joy kept me from the midday rest. Tamim al-Dari narrated to me, from some of his cousins, that they set out by sea from the direction of Syria, when a violent wind struck them and drove them to an island in the sea, where they found a beast with thick hair on its forelock. We said: What are you, O beast? It said: I am al-Jassasa. We said: Inform us. It said: I will neither inform you nor inquire of you anything, but in this monastery there is a man longing to inform you and to be informed by you. So we entered the monastery and found a one-eyed man bound in chains, showing grief and complaining much. When he saw us, he said: Have you followed? We informed him. He said: What has become of the Lake of Tiberias? We said: As it was, watering its people with its water and watering their crops. He said: What has become of the palm trees between Amman and Baysan? They said: They yield their fruit every year. He said: What has become of the spring of Zughar? They said: Its people drink from it and water their fields from it. He said: If these were to dry up, I would break free of these bonds and would not leave with these two feet of mine any watering place untrodden except Medina. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To this point my joy reached. Then he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no mountain pass of it except that an angel stands over it with drawn sword, turning him back from entering it. Al-Shabi said: I met al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayra, and he narrated it to me from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), adding in it: and Mecca. And he said: From the direction of the east, yet it is not from the direction of the east. Al-Shabi said: I met al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, and he narrated it to me from Aisha from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"373","Narrations of Asma bint Yazid ibn al-Sakan al-Ashhaliyya. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, that he heard Asma bint Yazid ibn Sakan saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us about the Dajjal, bringing his matter near, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I knead dough for my family, and I do not think it will finish before he emerges. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he emerges while I am among you, I will contend with him on your behalf, but if he emerges after me, then Allah is my successor over every Muslim."
"374","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Asma bint Yazid ibn Sakan, that he heard her saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me while I was among some women, and he greeted us, then said: Beware of ingratitude to benefactors. I said: What is ingratitude to benefactors? He said: Perhaps one of you remains long unmarried among her parents and grows old as a spinster, then Allah the Exalted provides her a husband and provides her from him wealth and children, then she becomes angry and denies it, saying: I never saw any good from you on any day at all."
"375","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, and Sufyan dropped from the Shaykh's book though it is indispensable, he said: Ibn Abi al-Husayn narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: I came to Asma bint Yazid, and she brought near to me a basket containing dates or fresh dates, and she said: Eat. I said: I do not desire it. She shouted at me, saying: Eat, for I am the one who adorned Aisha for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I brought her to him and seated her at his right, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a vessel containing milk, and he drank, then handed it to her, but she lowered her head out of shyness, so I said: Take from the hand of the Messenger of Allah, so she took it and drank. Then he said to her: Give to your companion. I said: Rather you drink, O Messenger of Allah, then hand to me. So he drank, then handed to me, and I turned the vessel to place my mouth where his mouth had been. Then he said: Give to your companions. They said: We do not desire it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine lying and hunger. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw upon one of them a bracelet of gold, and said: Would you like Allah the Exalted to encircle you in its place with bracelets of fire? She said: We crowded upon it until we removed it and threw it away, and we do not know where it is to this hour. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it not enough for one of you to take beads of silver, then take some saffron and dissolve it and smear it over them, so they look as if of gold."
"376","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Husayn narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, that he heard Asma bint Yazid saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among some women, and he said: In what you are able and capable of. We said: O Messenger of Allah, accept our pledge. He said: I do not shake hands with women; I only take upon you what Allah the Exalted took."
"377","Narrations of the men of the Ansar. Narration of Muadh ibn Jabal. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: One who was present with Muadh ibn Jabal when death came to him informed me, saying: Uncover the curtain of the tent from me so I may narrate to you a narration I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); nothing kept me from narrating it to you except that you might rely upon it and abandon deeds. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever says there is no god but Allah sincerely from his heart, or with certainty from his heart, will enter Paradise, and the Fire will not touch him."
"378","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan al-Ahwazi Abu Hammam narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Hissan ibn Kahil, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura, from Muadh ibn Jabal, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul that dies testifying that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, returning to a certain heart, except that Allah forgives him."
"379","Narrations of Ubayy ibn Kab. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us; Said ibn Jubayr informed me, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Nawf al-Bakkali claims that Musa, the companion of al-Khadir, is not Musa of the Children of Israel, but another Musa. Ibn Abbas said: The enemy of Allah has lied. Ubayy ibn Kab narrated to us that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Musa stood preaching among the Children of Israel and was asked: Which of the people is most knowledgeable? He said: I am most knowledgeable. So Allah the Exalted reproached him, since he did not refer knowledge back to Him. He said: I have a servant at the junction of the two seas who is more knowledgeable than you. Musa said: My Lord, how can I reach him? He said: Take a fish and place it in a basket, then set out; wherever you lose the fish, he is there. So he took a fish and placed it in a basket, then set out, and his servant Yusha ibn Nun set out with him, until when they reached the rock, they laid down their heads and slept. The fish stirred in the basket and came out of it, falling into the sea, taking its way into the sea as through a tunnel, and Allah the Exalted held back the flow of water from the fish, so it became like a vault over it. When Musa awoke, his companion forgot to inform him of the fish, and they continued the rest of their day and night, until on the morrow Musa said to his servant: Bring us our morning meal; we have suffered fatigue in this journey of ours. He said: Musa did not feel fatigue until he had passed the place Allah the Exalted had commanded him. His servant said to him: Did you see when we took refuge at the rock? I forgot the fish, and none made me forget to mention it but Satan, and it took its way into the sea in an amazing manner. He said: The fish had a tunnel-like path, while for Musa and his servant it was a wonder. Musa, peace be upon him, said: That is what we were seeking; so they retraced their steps. He said: They returned tracing their footsteps until they reached the rock, where there was a man wrapped in a garment. Musa greeted him, and al-Khadir said: How is peace in your land? He said: I am Musa. He said: Musa of the Children of Israel? He said: Yes; I have come to you that you may teach me of what you have been taught of right guidance. Al-Khadir said: You will never be able to have patience with me. O Musa, I am upon knowledge from the knowledge of Allah the Exalted which He taught me and you do not know, and you are upon knowledge from the knowledge of Allah the Exalted which Allah the Exalted taught you and I do not know. Musa said to him: You will find me, if Allah wills, patient, and I will not disobey you in any matter. Al-Khadir said: If you follow me, do not ask me about anything until I mention it to you. They set out walking along the seashore, and a ship passed them, and they asked its people to carry them; they recognized al-Khadir and carried them without fare. When they boarded the ship, Musa was taken by surprise when al-Khadir pulled out a plank of the ship's planks with an adze. Musa said: People carried us without fare, yet you deliberately damaged their ship, tearing it open to drown its people; you have done a grievous thing. Al-Khadir said: Did I not say that you will never be able to have patience with me? Musa said to him: Do not take me to task for what I forgot, and do not be hard upon me in my affair. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first of Musa's was forgetfulness. He said: A sparrow came and perched on the edge of the ship, pecking once into the sea, and al-Khadir said to him: My knowledge and your knowledge have not diminished the knowledge of Allah except as this sparrow has diminished this sea. Then they left the ship, and while they were walking along the shore, al-Khadir saw a boy playing among the boys, and al-Khadir seized his head and tore it off with his hand, killing him. Musa said to him: Have you killed an innocent soul without retribution? You have done a horrible thing. He said: Did I not say to you that you will never be able to have patience with me? And this was severer than the first. He said: If I ask you about anything after this, do not keep me company; you have received an excuse from me. He said: They set out until when they came to the people of a town, they asked its people for food, but they refused to host them, and they found therein a wall about to collapse, he said: leaning, and al-Khadir gestured with his hand like this and straightened it. Musa said: People we came to who neither fed us nor hosted us; if you wished you could have taken a wage for it. He said: This is parting between me and you; I will inform you of the interpretation of what you could not bear patiently. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We wished Musa, peace be upon him, had been patient so that more of their story would have been narrated to us. Said ibn Jubayr said: And Ibn Abbas used to recite: And before them was a king seizing every sound ship by force. And he used to recite: And as for the boy, he was a disbeliever, and his parents were believers."
"380","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Misar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara al-Zarrad, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying the Exalted: And their father was righteous. He said: He preserved them through the righteousness of their father, without mentioning any righteousness of theirs."
"381","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Suqa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: Allah the Exalted preserves, through the preservation of the righteous man, his child and his grandchild, the dwelling he is in and the dwellings around him; they remain under the protection of Allah the Exalted. Sufyan said: And he added in it for me: and a covering."
"382","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abda ibn Abi Lubaba and Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us that they heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh saying: I asked Ubayy ibn Kab about the two Muawwidhas, saying: O Abu al-Mundhir, your brother Ibn Masud erases them from the mushaf. He said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: It was said to me: Say, so I said. So we say as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"383","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abda ibn Abi Lubaba and Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us that they heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh saying: I said to Ubayy: Your brother Ibn Masud says: Whoever stands the whole year will attain the Night of Decree. He said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman; he only meant that people should not rely upon it, yet he knew that it is in the last ten of Ramadan, and that it is the night of the twenty-seventh. Then Ubayy swore without exception: It is the night of the twenty-seventh. We said to him: O Abu al-Mundhir, by what did you know it? He said: By the sign or mark the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us of. He informed us: That the sun rises on the morning of that day without rays."
"384","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: I had a cousin living far away, and I said: If only you would take a house near the mosque, or a donkey. He said: I would not like my house to be joined to the house of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I never heard from him, since he embraced Islam, a word harder upon me than it, yet he was speaking of the footsteps. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he said: He has for every step he takes to the mosque a degree."
"385","Narrations of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: And Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi informed me that he heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to shun his brother for more than three days; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting. Sufyan said: al-Zuhri had narrated to us before it the narration of Anas, then followed it with this, saying: So Ata ibn Yazid informed me."
"386","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi informed me, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qibla with stool or urine, nor turn your backs to it, but face east or west. Abu Ayyub said: We came to Syria and found privies built facing the qibla, so we turn aside and seek Allah the Exalted's forgiveness. It was said to Sufyan: But Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi does not trace it to the Prophet. He said: But I memorized it and trace it as I told you. Then he said: The Meccans only took a book brought by Humayd al-Araj from Syria, written from al-Zuhri, which fell to Ibn Jurayj; the Meccans would present that book to Ibn Shihab, but as for us, we only heard from his mouth."
"387","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn informed me, from his father, who said: Ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama disputed at al-Arj about a pilgrim washing his head, so they sent me to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. I went to him and found him between the two posts of the well, washing himself; when he saw me coming, he gathered his garments to his chest until I looked at him, and I said: Your nephew Ibn Abbas sent me to you asking how you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washing his head while in pilgrim sanctity? He moved his hands over his head, bringing them forward and back, saying: Like this, like this. So I returned to them and informed them. Al-Miswar said to Ibn Abbas: I will never dispute with you again."
"388","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Said narrated to us, from Umar ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from Abu Ayyub, who said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year. Abu Bakr said: I said to Sufyan, or it was said to him: They trace it to the Prophet. He said: Be silent about it; I know that."
"389","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym and Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year."
"390","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Saigh narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"391","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Maghrib and Isha together at Muzdalifa."
"392","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Sad al-Ama narrating to Ata ibn Abi Rabah, saying: Abu Ayyub went out to Uqba ibn Amir while he was in Egypt, asking him about a narration he had heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with none left who had heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except him and Uqba. When he arrived, he came to the house of Maslama ibn Mukhallad al-Ansari, the governor of Egypt, who was informed of him, so he hastened out to him and embraced him, then said: What brought you, O Abu Ayyub? He said: A narration I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with none left who heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except me and Uqba, so send one to guide me to his house. He sent with him one to guide him to Uqba's house, and Uqba was informed of him, so he hastened out to him, embracing him, saying: What brought you, O Abu Ayyub? He said: A narration I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with none left who heard it except me and you, concerning concealing the believer. Uqba said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever conceals a believer in the world over a disgrace, Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Ayyub said to him: You spoke the truth. Then Abu Ayyub left for his mount and rode it back to Medina, and the gift of Maslama ibn Mukhallad only reached him at Arish of Egypt."
"393","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ubayda al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qazaa, from al-Qartha, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would, when the sun declined, pray four and say: The gates of heaven, or of Paradise, are opened at the sun's decline."
"394","Narrations of Ubada ibn al-Samit. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: I heard Mahmud ibn al-Rabi narrating, from Ubada ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer for one who does not recite in it the Opening of the Book."
"395","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Abu Idris al-Khawlani informed me that he heard Ubada ibn al-Samit saying: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a gathering, and he said: Pledge to me that you will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery. The verse: Whoever of you fulfills it, his reward is upon Allah; whoever commits any of that and is punished for it, it is expiation for him; and whoever commits any of that and Allah the Exalted conceals it for him, then he is left to Allah the Exalted: if He wills He forgives him, and if He wills He punishes him. Sufyan said: We were with al-Zuhri, and when he narrated this narration, Abu Bakr al-Hudhali gestured to me to memorize it, so I wrote it; when al-Zuhri stood up, I informed Abu Bakr of it."
"396","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari and Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from al-Mukhdaji, who said: It was said to Ubada ibn al-Samit: Abu Muhammad says the witr is obligatory. Ubada said: Abu Muhammad has erred. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Five prayers Allah has prescribed upon the servants in the day and night; whoever performs them without diminishing any of their rights, for those able, it is a right upon Allah the Exalted to admit him to Paradise, and whoever does not perform them has no covenant with Allah: if He wills He forgives him, and if He wills He punishes him."
"397","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: I heard Ubada ibn al-Walid narrating, from Ubada ibn al-Samit, who said: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey in hardship and ease, in activity and reluctance, not to dispute authority with its people, and to speak the truth wherever we are, fearing for Allah the Exalted the blame of no blamer."
"398","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Ubada ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, like for like, silver for silver, like for like, dates for dates, like for like, wheat for wheat, like for like, barley for barley, like for like, until he specified salt for salt: Whoever adds or seeks addition, it is usury."
"399","Narrations of Abu al-Darda. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Abu Salih, from Ata ibn Yasar, from a man of Egypt, who said: I asked Abu al-Darda about the saying of Allah the Exalted: Those who believed and were pious, for them are glad tidings in the life of the world and in the Hereafter. He said: None asked me about it since I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it except you, apart from one man. I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about it, and he said: None asked me about it since it was revealed except you, apart from one man: the righteous dream a Muslim sees or is seen for him."
"400","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan said: Then I met Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, and he narrated it to me, from Abu Salih, from Ata ibn Yasar, from a man of Egypt, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"401","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Yala ibn Mamlak, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given his share of gentleness has been given his share of good, and whoever is deprived of his share of gentleness has been deprived of his share of good."
"402","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Yala ibn Mamlak, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heaviest thing in the balance is good character, and Allah the Exalted hates the foul-mouthed and obscene."
"403","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abu al-Darda, that a man came to him and said to him: My father commands me to divorce her. Abu al-Darda said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The father is the middle gate of Paradise, so lose it or preserve it. And Sufyan would sometimes say: My mother, and sometimes say: My mother or my father."
"404","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, who said: I recited in Syria: By the night when it covers, and the day when it shines, and the male and the female. Abu al-Darda said: Is this how you heard Abdullah reciting it? I said: Yes. He said: He testifies that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting it thus: and the male and the female."
"405","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Sadi, who said: I asked Said ibn al-Musayyib about eating hyena. He said: Does anyone eat it? I said: Some of my people snare them and eat them. Said said: Eating it is not proper. An elder with him said: Shall I not inform you of what I heard from Abu al-Darda? I heard Abu al-Darda saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade all plunder, all snatching, animals tied up and shot at, and every beast with fangs."
"406","Narrations of Zayd ibn Thabit al-Ansari. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us that he heard Tawus narrating, from Hujr al-Madari, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed the umra gift for the heir."
"407","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, who said: And Zayd ibn Thabit informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of araya."
"408","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Sad al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit came to us while we were in a garden setting traps for birds, and he drove us away, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hunting in Medina."
"409","Narrations of Sahl ibn Abi Hathma. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim informed me, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathma, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays toward a sutra, let him draw near to it, so that Satan does not cut off his prayer."
"410","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Bushayr ibn Yasar, freedman of Ibn Haritha, informed me, he said: I heard Sahl ibn Abi Hathma saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit for dates, except that he permitted the ariya to be sold by its estimate, its people eating it as fresh dates."
"411","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Bushayr ibn Yasar informed me that he heard Sahl ibn Abi Hathma saying: Abdullah ibn Sahl was found slain in a waterless well or well of the wells of Khaybar, so his brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl and his uncles Huwayyisa and Muhayyisa, sons of Masud, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abd al-Rahman went to speak, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The elder, the elder. So Muhayyisa spoke, mentioning the killing of Abdullah ibn Sahl, saying: O Messenger of Allah, we found Abdullah ibn Sahl slain, and the Jews are people of disbelief and treachery; they are the ones who killed him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you swear fifty oaths and become entitled to your companion, or the blood of your companion. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can we swear upon what we were not present for and did not witness? He said: Then the Jews will absolve themselves with fifty oaths. They said: How can we accept the oaths of a polytheist people? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money from his own funds. Sahl said: A young she-camel of them kicked me."
"412","Narrations of Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Amash saying: I heard Shaqiq ibn Salama Abu Wail saying: On the day of Siffin, when the two arbiters arbitrated, I heard Sahl ibn Hunayf saying: O people, suspect your judgment; we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Abu Jandal, and if we could have rejected the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would have rejected it. By Allah, we have not placed our swords upon our shoulders since we embraced Islam for a distressing matter except that it led us easily to a matter we recognize, yet this matter, by Allah, no breach in it is closed except that another breach opens upon us."
"413","Narrations of Rafi ibn Khadij al-Ansari. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: We used to sharecrop and saw no harm in it, until Rafi ibn Khadij claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it, so we abandoned it because of his saying."
"414","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hanzala ibn Qays al-Zuraqi informed me that he heard Rafi ibn Khadij saying: We were the Ansar with the most fields, and we would say to the one we sharecropped with: This portion is yours and this portion is ours, which he cultivates for us; sometimes this would yield and this would not, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that, but with silver he did not forbid us. It was said to Sufyan: But Malik narrates it from Rabia, from Hanzala? He said: What would he hope for with it when it is with Yahya; Yahya is the more careful of the two, but we memorized it from Yahya."
"415","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, that a slave stole young palm shoots from a man's garden and brought them, planting them in his family's garden, and he was brought to Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who wanted to cut his hand, so Rafi ibn Khadij testified that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting for fruit or palm pith. So Marwan released him."
"416","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Karim narrated to us: The name of the one who stole was Fil."
"417","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatada, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray Fajr at dawn brightness, for that is greater for the reward. Or he said: for your rewards."
"418","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq narrated to us, from his father, from Abaya ibn Rifaa ibn Rafi, from Rafi ibn Khadij, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we will meet the enemy tomorrow and have no knives with us; shall we slaughter with reeds? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever causes blood to flow and Allah's name is mentioned over it, eat it, except what is of tooth or nail; for the tooth is a bone of man, and the nail is the knife of the Abyssinians."
"419","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq narrated to us, from his father, from Abaya ibn Rifaa, from Rafi ibn Khadij, who said: We captured camels and sheep, and we would equate a camel with ten sheep. A camel of them bolted from us, so we shot it with arrows. Then we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: These camels have wildness like the wildness of game; when any of them bolts, do thus with it and eat it. Sufyan said: And Ismail ibn Muslim added in it: We shot it with arrows until we pinned it down."
"420","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us: From Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from his father, from Abaya, from Rafi ibn Khadij, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave on the day of Hunayn to Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, Safwan ibn Umayya, Uyayna ibn Hisn, and al-Aqra ibn Habis one hundred camels, and gave Abbas ibn Mirdas less than that. Then Sufyan said: Umar or another said in this narration that Abbas ibn Mirdas spoke, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) completed one hundred for him."
"421","Narrations of Abdullah ibn Zayd al-Ansari, who was shown the call to prayer. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abbad ibn Tamim informed me, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, who said: A man complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that something is imagined to him in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell. And Sufyan would sometimes say: Let him not turn away."
"422","Narrations of Abu Qatada al-Ansari. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf informed me, he said: I used to see a dream that would make me shiver, though I would not be covered up, and I came to Abu Qatada and complained of that to him, and he narrated to me that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The good dream is from Allah, and the bad dream is from Satan; when one of you sees a bad dream he dislikes, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from the evil of what he saw, for it will not harm him."
"423","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: And four narrated it to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talha, Abd Rabbihi and Yahya, sons of Said, and Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqama, that they heard it from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrating it from Abu Qatada: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The righteous dream is from Allah, and the bad dream is from Satan; when one of you sees a bad dream he dislikes, let him blow to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from the evil of what he saw, for it will not harm him."
"424","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, without mentioning the beginning of the narration as al-Zuhri mentioned it, and al-Zuhri is more retentive than all of them."
"425","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman and Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us that they heard Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrating from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Abu Qatada al-Ansari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you enters the mosque, let him pray two rakahs before sitting."
"426","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman and Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us that they heard Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr informing from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi, from Abu Qatada, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leading the people while Umama bint Abi al-As, daughter of Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), was upon his shoulder; when he bowed he put her down, and when he finished prostration he took her up again."
"427","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Abu Muhammad, from Abu Qatada, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awarded me the spoils of a slain man I had killed on the day of Hunayn. Sufyan said: The narration is long, and I memorized of it this."
"428","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Muhammad saying: I heard Abu Qatada saying: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when we were at al-Qaha, some of us in pilgrim sanctity and others not, I saw my companions looking at something, so I looked and saw a wild ass. I saddled my horse and mounted, took my spear, but my whip fell. I said to my companions: Hand it to me, but they were in pilgrim sanctity, so they said: By Allah, we will not help you against it with anything. So I picked up my whip, then came to the ass from behind it while it was beyond a hillock, and thrust it with my spear, hamstringing it, and brought it to my companions. Some said: Eat it. Others said: Do not eat it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was ahead of us, so I spurred my horse and caught up with him, and asked him, and he said: It is lawful, so eat it."
"429","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qays informed me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada, from his father, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I strike with this sword of mine in the path of Allah until I am killed, patient, seeking reward, advancing, not retreating; will Allah expiate my sins? He said: Yes. Then he was silent a while, until I thought something was being revealed to him. When the man turned away, he said: Come; this is Jibril saying: Except that there is a debt upon you."
"430","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"431","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me."
"432","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to touch his private part with his right hand. Sufyan said: Meaning in cleaning after relieving oneself."
"433","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Abu Qazaa, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Harmala, from Abu Qatada, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting the day of Arafa expiates this year and the year following it, and fasting Ashura expiates a year. Sufyan said: Dawud said: And Ata would not fast it until this narration reached him."
"434","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha narrated to me, he said: I heard a woman, I think the wife of Abdullah ibn Abi Qatada, Sufyan doubting, that Abu Qatada would come to them and perform ablution with them, tilting the vessel for the cat to drink from, and we asked him about its leftover? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that it is not impure, saying: It is among those that go around you, male and female."
"435","Narrations of Abu Talha al-Ansari. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba informed me, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Talha al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angel does not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"436","Narrations of Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying concerning a man going to relieve himself: Can none of you find three stones? Hisham said: And Abu Wajza informed me, from Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no dung in them."
"437","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us similarly from Hisham, except that he said: from Abu Khuzayma, from Umara."
"438","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted us to wipe over the leather socks for three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and night for the resident; had we asked him for more, he would have given us more."
"439","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, except that he said: Had the questioner been profuse in his questioning, he would have given him more."
"440","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usama ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"441","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us similarly from Hisham, except that he said: from Abu Khuzayma, from Umara."
"442","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted us to wipe over the leather socks for three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and night for the resident; had we asked him for more, he would have given us more."
"443","Al-Humaydi narrated to us: Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly, except that he said: Had the questioner been profuse in his questioning, he would have given him more."
"444","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usama ibn al-Had narrated to us, from Umara ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"445","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, saying: Bushayr ibn Yasar informed me, saying: I heard Suwayd ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Khaybar until, when we were at al-Sahba, and between us and it was a short distance, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for provisions, and nothing was brought but sawiq. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chewed it, and we chewed it along with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rinsed his mouth, and we rinsed along with him. Then he led us in the Maghrib prayer, and we prayed with him, and he did not perform ablution."
"446","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Jami' ibn Abi Rashid, Abd al-Malik ibn A'yan, and Asim ibn Bahdalah narrated to us that they heard it from Abu Wa'il, saying: I heard Qays ibn Abi Gharazah say: We used to be called brokers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to us while we were at al-Baqi' with sticks in our hands, and he gave us a name better than it, saying: O company of merchants. So we gathered to him, and he said: This selling is attended by swearing and lying, so mix it with charity."
"447","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shumaylah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Mihsan al-Ansari, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you wakes up secure among his people, healthy in his body, with the food of his day at hand, it is as if the world had been gathered for him."
"448","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Farwah al-Juhani narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Ukaym say: We were with Hudhayfah at al-Mada'in when he asked a dihqan for water, and he brought him water in a silver vessel. Hudhayfah threw it away — and he was a man with sharpness in him — and they disliked speaking to him. Then he turned to the people and said: I apologize to you for this; I had instructed him not to give me drink in this. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and said: Do not drink from vessels of gold and silver, and do not wear dibaj and silk, for it is for them in this world and for you in the Hereafter."
"449","Sufyan said: And Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: We were with Hudhayfah, and he mentioned the like of it exactly."
"450","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mansur narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night, he would rub his mouth with the siwak."
"451","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Wa'il say: I heard Hudhayfah say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to the rubbish heap of a people and urinate standing. I started to move away from him, but he drew me to him until I was at his heels. When he finished, he performed ablution and wiped over his khuffs."
"452","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Nakha'i, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: We were with Hudhayfah when a man passed by us, and it was said to Hudhayfah: This is a man who carries reports to the rulers. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The talebearer shall not enter Paradise. Sufyan said: And al-qattat is the slanderer."
"453","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to sleep, he would place his hand under his head and then say: O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You gather — or resurrect — Your servants."
"454","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Nudhayr, from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of the lower part of the muscle of my calf — or his calf — and said: This is the place of the izar; if you refuse, then lower; if you refuse, then lower; if you refuse, then the izar has no right to what is below the ankles."
"455","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, and he was most firm in this hadith, saying: Zayd ibn Wahb informed me, saying: I heard Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us two hadiths; I have seen one of them, and I am awaiting the other. He narrated to us: Trustworthiness descended into the roots of men's hearts, then the Qur'an came down, so they learned from the Qur'an and learned from the Sunnah. Then he narrated to us about its removal, saying: A man sleeps a slumber and trustworthiness is taken from his heart, and its trace remains like the trace of a speck; then he sleeps and trustworthiness is taken from his heart, and its trace remains like the trace of a blister. Then he took pebbles and rolled them on his leg, saying: Like an ember you rolled on your leg, so it blistered, and you see it swollen with nothing in it. And people will go on trading with not a man among them fulfilling trust, until it is said of a man: How strong he is, how clever, how intelligent — while there is not the weight of a mustard seed of faith in his heart. I used to care not whom I traded with: if he was a Muslim, his Islam would return my due to me, and if he was a Jew or a Christian, his agent would return it to me; and today I trade only with so-and-so."
"456","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Jami' ibn Abi Rashid and Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Who will narrate to us about the tribulation? I said: I heard him say: A man's trial in his family, his wealth, and his neighbor is expiated by prayer, charity, and fasting. Umar said: I am not asking you about that; I am asking you about the one that surges like the surge of the sea. I said: Before it there is a closed door — the killing of a man, or his death. He said: Will that door be broken or opened? I said: No, rather it will be broken. Umar said: That is more likely never to be closed until the Day of Resurrection. Al-A'mash narrated to us, and we feared to ask Hudhayfah whether Umar knew that he was the door, so we instructed Masruq and he asked him. He said: Yes, just as you know that before tomorrow there is tonight; that is because I narrated to him a hadith free of confusion."
"457","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, who said: I said to Hudhayfah: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in Bayt al-Maqdis? Hudhayfah said: You say he prayed in it, O bald one? I said: Yes; between me and you is the Qur'an. Hudhayfah said: Bring it; whoever argues by the Qur'an has prevailed. So I recited to him: Glory to Him who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque. Hudhayfah said to me: Where do you find that he prayed in it? Had he prayed in it, prayer in it would have been prescribed for you as prayer in the Sacred Mosque was prescribed. Then Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a beast with a long extended back called al-Buraq, its stride as far as the eye can see, and the two of them did not leave the back of al-Buraq until they saw Paradise and Hell and the whole promise of the Hereafter. And they narrate that he tied it up — would it flee from him? Rather, the Knower of the unseen and the seen had made it subservient to him."
"458","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Za'idah ibn Qudamah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow the two after me: Abu Bakr and Umar; be guided by the guidance of Ammar; and hold to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd."
"459","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us that he heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrating, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, Uqbah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the fee of a soothsayer."
"460","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz delayed the prayer one day, and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril descended and led me, so I prayed with him; then he descended and led me, so I prayed with him; then he descended and led me, so I prayed with him, until he counted the five prayers. Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said to him: Fear Allah, O Urwah, and consider what you say. Urwah said: Bashir ibn Abi Mas'ud informed me of it, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"461","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Alqamah, from Abu Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him. Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid said: Then I met Abu Mas'ud in the tawaf and asked him about it, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the two verses from the end of Surah al-Baqarah in a night, they suffice him."
"462","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, saying: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim say: I heard Abu Mas'ud say: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I stay away from the dawn prayer because of how long so-and-so makes it for us. He said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) angrier in an exhortation than his anger that day. Then he said: Among you are those who repel; among you are those who repel. So whichever of you leads the people, let him lighten, for among them are the old, the sick, the weak, and the one with a need."
"463","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abu Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer suffices in which a man does not straighten his back in bowing and prostration. Sufyan said: Thus al-A'mash said it."
"464","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, saying: I heard Qays say: I heard Abu Mas'ud say: The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, and the people said: The sun has eclipsed for the death of Ibrahim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are two signs from the signs of Allah; they are not eclipsed for the death or life of anyone. So when you see that, hasten to the remembrance of Allah and to prayer."
"465","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abu Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten our shoulders in prayer, saying: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ; and let those of understanding and maturity be nearest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them."
"466","Sufyan said: We memorized it from al-A'mash, and we did not find it here in Makkah. He said: I heard Isma'il ibn Raja' narrating, from Aws ibn Dam'aj al-Hadrami, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people are led by the most versed of them in the Book of Allah; if they are equal in recitation, then the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah; if they are equal in the Sunnah, then the earliest of them in hijrah; if they are equal in hijrah, then the eldest of them. And no man shall be led in his domain, nor sat upon his honored seat in his house, except by his permission."
"467","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Coarseness, hardness, and harshness of hearts are among the loud-voiced herdsmen of the wabar, at the roots of the tails of camels, from Rabi'ah and Mudar."
"468","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Kathir ibn Abbas narrated to me, from his father, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on his mule which the Judhami had gifted to him. When the Muslims turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abbas, call out, saying: O companions of the samurah tree; O companions of Surah al-Baqarah. And I was a loud-voiced man, so I said: O companions of the samurah; O companions of Surah al-Baqarah. They returned with a turning like the turning of cows to their calves, voices rose, and they were saying: O company of the Ansar; O company of the Ansar. Then the call was narrowed to Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: O Banu al-Harith. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stretched himself up while on his mule, saying: This is when battle has heated. And he was saying: Forward, O Abbas. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took pebbles and threw them, then said: They are defeated, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. And Sufyan would sometimes say: By the Lord of Muhammad. Sufyan said: al-Zuhri narrated it to us at length, and this is what I retained of it."
"469","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal say: I heard al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib say: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talib used to protect you and support you, so did that benefit him? He said: Yes; I found him in the depths of the Fire, and I brought him out to its shallow edge."
"470","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication with which to supplicate. He said: O Abbas, ask Allah for pardon and well-being. He said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication with which to supplicate. He said: O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for pardon and well-being. He said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication with which to supplicate. He said: O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. Abu Bakr al-Humaydi said: And Sufyan would sometimes say in this hadith, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, that al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, and most often he would say, from al-Abbas, that he said: O Messenger of Allah."
"471","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Harmalah narrated to us, saying: Kurayb narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Fadl ibn Abbas — and he was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Muzdalifah until he stoned the Jamarah — who said: I kept hearing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) utter the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamarah."
"472","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I was among the weak of his household whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead from Muzdalifah to Mina."
"473","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: Ata informed me, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"474","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar, Sufyan al-Thawri, and others narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ahead the young boys of Banu Abd al-Muttalib from Muzdalifah to Mina, and he kept patting our thighs, saying: My little sons, do not stone Jamarat al-Aqabah until the sun rises."
"475","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a man fell from his camel, his neck was broken, and he died while in ihram. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote, shroud him in his two garments, and do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection uttering the talbiyah — or he said: saying labbayk."
"476","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim Abu Hurrah al-Nasibi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it. And he added in it: And do not bring perfume near him."
"477","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'bad informed me, and he was among the most truthful freedmen of Ibn Abbas, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching, saying: No man shall be alone with a woman, and it is not lawful for a woman to travel except with a mahram. A man stood up to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have been enlisted for such-and-such expedition, while my wife has set out for Hajj. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and perform Hajj with your wife. Sufyan said: The Kufans would always come to Amr asking him about this hadith, saying: How is the hadith of: I was enlisted for such-and-such expedition?"
"478","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Sha'tha, Jabir ibn Zayd, informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever finds no sandals, let him wear khuffs, and whoever finds no izar, let him wear trousers — meaning while in ihram."
"479","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Zayd informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah eight together and seven together. I said to him: O Abu al-Sha'tha, I suppose he delayed the Zuhr and hastened the Asr, and delayed the Maghrib and hastened the Isha. He said: And I suppose so too."
"480","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zubayr informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, without travel or fear, eight together and seven together. I said: Why did he do that? He said: I said: He wanted not to burden his ummah."
"481","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Kurayb informed me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I spent a night at my aunt Maymunah's. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose at night and performed a light ablution from a hanging waterskin — and he described it, making little of it — so I got up and did the like of what he did, then I came and stood at his left. He moved me behind him and placed me at his right. He prayed, then lay down and slept until he snored. Then Bilal came to him and announced the prayer to him, so he went out and prayed without performing ablution."
"482","Sufyan said: And Ibn Jurayj narrated it to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, the like of it up to his saying: He moved me behind him and placed me at his right, then he prayed. Amr ibn Dinar, who was in the gathering, said to him: Come on, add more, O Abu Muhammad. Ata said: What addition? This is how I heard it. Amr said: Rather, Kurayb informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that he said: Then he lay down and slept until he snored. Then Bilal came to him and announced the prayer to him, so he prayed without performing ablution. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan said: This is for the Prophet specifically, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): his eye sleeps but his heart does not sleep."
"483","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan said: And Amr narrated to us that he heard Ubayd ibn Umayr say: The dreams of the prophets are revelation. And he recited: I see in sleep that I am sacrificing you."
"484","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, and I retained it from him, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I and al-Fadl came on a she-ass while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Arafah. We passed by part of the row, dismounted, left it to graze, and entered into the prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said nothing to us."
"485","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I bear witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he prayed before the sermon on the day of Eid. Then he preached, saw that he had not made the women hear, so he came to them, exhorted them, reminded them, and commanded them to give charity, with Bilal alongside him holding out his garment like this — Abu Bakr said: as if receiving with his garment — and the woman began to throw her ring, her earring, and such things."
"486","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, saying: I heard Ikrimah say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in Sad, though it is not among the obligatory prostrations."
"487","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Huwayrith say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came out from relieving himself and food was brought to him. It was said to him: Will you not perform ablution? He said: Am I to pray, that I should perform ablution?"
"488","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, that Umar went to relieve himself, then came out and food was brought to him. It was said to him: Will you not perform ablution? He said: I only clean myself with my left, and I only eat with my right."
"489","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'bad informed me, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: We did not know the end of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by the takbir. Amr said: I later mentioned it to Abu Ma'bad, and he denied it, saying: I did not narrate it to you. I said: Indeed, you narrated it to me before this. Sufyan said: As if he feared for himself."
"490","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) order a bucket from Zamzam; it was drawn for him, and he drank while standing."
"491","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an narrated to us, from Umar ibn Harmalah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: I entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon my aunt Maymunah, and with us was Khalid ibn al-Walid. Maymunah said to him: Shall we not offer you, O Messenger of Allah, something Umm Uqayq gifted us? She brought him roasted lizards. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them, he spat three times and did not eat of them, and he ordered us to eat. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a vessel with milk, and he drank while I was at his right and Khalid at his left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: The drink is yours, O boy, though if you wish you may prefer Khalid with it. I said: I would not prefer anyone with the leftover of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah feeds with food, let him say: O Allah, bless it for us and replace it with what is better than it; and whomever Allah gives milk to drink, let him say: O Allah, bless it for us and increase us of it; for I know nothing that suffices in place of food and drink but it."
"492","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching on the minbar, saying: You will meet Allah walking barefoot, naked, uncircumcised."
"493","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I did not know the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to fast a day seeking its merit over other days except this day — meaning the day of Ashura — and this month — meaning the month of Ramadan."
"494","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I remain alive, I shall order fasting a day before it or a day after it — meaning the day of Ashura."
"495","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us that he heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Wa'lah al-Misri say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any hide that is tanned has become pure."
"496","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Shaybani narrated to us, saying: I entered the mosque with al-Sha'bi, and he said: Do you see anyone of our companions to sit with? Do you see Abu Husayn? I said: No. Then he looked and saw Yazid ibn al-Asamm, and said: Would you sit with him? His aunt is Maymunah. So we sat with him, and Yazid ibn al-Asamm said: There was mentioned in the presence of Ibn Abbas the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the lizard: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it. He became angry and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent only permitting or forbidding, and it was eaten in his presence."
"497","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ammar al-Duhni and Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Jabir narrated to us that they heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd say: A man came to Ibn Abbas and asked him about a man who killed a believer deliberately, then repented, believed, did righteous deeds, then was guided. Ibn Abbas said: And how is guidance for him? I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The slain shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection clinging to the killer, his jugular veins gushing blood, until he is brought to the Throne, and he says: Lord, ask this one for what he killed me. Ibn Abbas said: By Allah, Allah sent it down upon His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then He never abrogated it since He sent it down."
"498","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Suhaym, the freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Ma'bad ibn Abbas informed me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lifted the curtain while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr, and said: Nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream, which the Muslim sees or which is seen for him. Verily I have been forbidden to recite while bowing or prostrating. As for bowing, glorify the Lord therein; and as for prostration, strive in supplication, for it is worthy that it be answered for you. Sufyan said: Ziyad ibn Sa'd informed me of it before I heard it, and I said to him: Shall I convey your greeting of peace to Sulayman? He said: Yes. When I came to Madinah, I conveyed his greeting to him and asked him about it."
"499","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn Abi Rabah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hands until he licks them or has them licked. Sufyan said: Amr ibn Qays said to him: O Abu Muhammad, Ata only narrated it to us from Jabir. Amr said: By Allah, I heard it from Ata narrating it from Ibn Abbas before Jabir came to us in Makkah. Sufyan said: Amr and Ata met Jabir, if Allah wills, in a year in which he stayed as a mujawir."
"500","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a sheep belonging to a freedwoman of Maymunah, which she had been given from charity, dead. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is upon its people if they took its hide, tanned it, and benefited from it? They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is dead. He said: Only eating it is forbidden. And Sufyan would sometimes mention Maymunah in it and sometimes not mention her; so we mention it thus and thus."
"501","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ata. And Ibn Jurayj narrated it to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said — Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha one night. Umar went out and said: The prayer, O Messenger of Allah; the women and children have slept. Amr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out with his head dripping water, saying: It is indeed the time, were it not that I would burden the believers I would not pray it except at this hour. Ibn Jurayj said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha one night, then came out with his head dripping water, saying: It is indeed the time, were it not that I would burden the believers I would not pray it except at this hour. Ibn Jurayj said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out wiping water from his side, saying: It is indeed the time, were it not that I would burden my ummah. And Sufyan would sometimes narrate this hadith merging it from Ibn Abbas, from Amr and Ibn Jurayj, without mentioning the report therein; but when he said therein: narrated to us and I heard, or I heard, or informed us, he narrated this upon this, and this upon this."
"502","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: I heard Tawus narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate upon seven, and he was forbidden to tuck up his hair or his clothes."
"503","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Tawus narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate upon seven: upon his hands, his knees, the tips of his toes, and his forehead; and he was forbidden, if Allah wills, to tuck up the hair and the clothes. Sufyan said: And Ibn Tawus showed us, placing his hand on his forehead then passing it until he reached the tip of his nose; and my father used to count this as one."
"504","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu Umayyah Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq narrated to us, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones, and he was commanded not to tuck up hair nor garment."
"505","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Ahwal, the maternal uncle of Ibn Abi Najih, narrated to us, saying: I heard Tawus say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at night to pray tahajjud, he would say: O Allah, to You is praise; You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and all in them; to You is praise, You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth and all in them; to You is praise, You are the King of the heavens and the earth and all in them; to You is praise, You are the Truth, Your promise is truth, Your meeting is truth, Paradise is truth, Hell is truth, the Hour is truth, Muhammad is truth, and the prophets are truth. O Allah, to You I have submitted, in You I have believed, upon You I have relied, to You I have turned, by You I have disputed, to You I have brought judgment. So forgive me what I have done before and after, what I have hidden and declared. You are the Advancer and You are the Delayer; there is no god but You — or he said: there is no god but You. Sufyan doubted. And Abd al-Karim added in it: And there is no power nor strength except through You — which Sulayman did not say."
"506","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talhah, narrated to us, saying: Kurayb Abu Rashdin narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from the house of Juwayriyah after praying the dawn — her name had been Barrah, so he named her Juwayriyah, disliking that it be said: He went out from Barrah. Ibn Abbas said: He went out from her after praying the dawn, then returned to her after the day had risen while she was sitting in her place of prayer, and said to her: Have you remained in this seat of yours? She said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I said after you four words three times; had they been weighed against all you have said, they would outweigh them: Glory be to Allah and with His praise, by the number of His creation, the pleasure of Himself, the weight of His Throne, and the ink of His words."
"507","Concerning Hajj: Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: I heard Ata narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only hastened around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah to show the polytheists his strength."
"508","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Muhassab is nothing; it is only a stop where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped."
"509","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated this hadith, and Hisham ibn Urwah narrated concerning al-Muhassab, and Salih ibn Kaysan narrated; these hadiths were narrated to us by these, and there is not in them the like of it."
"510","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us this hadith twice: once he said in it: I heard Ata say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram."
"511","And once I heard him say: I heard Tawus narrating from Ibn Abbas, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram; and I do not know whether Amr heard it from both of them or whether one of the two times was a mistake."
"512","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram."
"513","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Ahwal narrated to us, saying: I heard Tawus narrating from Ibn Abbas, who said: People used to depart in every direction, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None shall depart until his last covenant is with the House. Sufyan said: I never heard in this hadith anything better than this which Sulayman narrated to us."
"514","Sufyan said: And Ibn Tawus informed us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: People were commanded that their last covenant be with the House, except that it was lightened for the menstruating woman."
"515","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Sha'tha informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram. Abu al-Sha'tha said: Whom do you think, O Amr? I said: They claim she is Maymunah. Abu al-Sha'tha said: Ibn Abbas informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram."
"516","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, the brother of Musa ibn Uqbah, narrated to me, saying: I heard Kurayb narrating that he heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out on return; when he was at al-Rawha he met a caravan, greeted them, and they returned his greeting. He said: Who are the people? They said: The Muslims; and who are the people? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the Messenger of Allah. A woman hastened to him, lifting to him a boy of hers from a litter, saying: O Messenger of Allah, does this one have Hajj? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, and for you is reward. Sufyan said: And Ibn al-Munkadir had first narrated it to us mursal; it was said to me: He only heard it from Ibrahim. So I went to Ibrahim and asked him about it, and he narrated it to me, saying: I narrated it to Ibn al-Munkadir, and he performed Hajj with all his family."
"517","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, saying: It was said to Ibn al-Munkadir: Do you perform Hajj while debt is upon you? He said: Hajj is a better settler of debt."
"518","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me, from his father, that it was said to him: Do you perform Hajj with children? He said: Yes; I present them to Allah."
"519","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard Sulayman ibn Yasar say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: A woman from Khath'am asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the morning of the Sacrifice, with al-Fadl riding behind him: The obligation of Allah in Hajj upon His servants has overtaken my father while he is a very old man unable to hold himself on the mount; do you see that we may perform Hajj for him? He said: Yes. Sufyan said: And Amr ibn Dinar had first narrated it to us from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, adding in it: I said: O Messenger of Allah, will that benefit him? He said: Yes, just as if one of you had a debt and paid it. When al-Zuhri came to us, I checked it and he did not say it."
"520","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: Tawus informed me, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas say: As for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, it is food: that it be sold until it is taken into possession. And Sufyan would sometimes say: until it is measured. Ibn Abbas said by his opinion: And I do not consider anything but the like of it."
"521","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: I said to Tawus: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, if you left sharecropping, for they claim the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it. He said: O Amr, the most knowledgeable of them about that — meaning Ibn Abbas — informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it, but said: That one of you grants his brother his land is better for him than that he take a fixed rent for it. And Mu'adh, when he came to Yemen, kept them upon it; and I — meaning Amr — help them and give them: if they profit, it is for me and for them, and if they lose, it is upon me and upon them. And al-haqalah is among the Ansar, so ask about it. So I asked Ali ibn Rifa'ah, and he said: It is sharecropping."
"522","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Kathir al-Dari, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while they were advancing payment for dates for two and three years. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever advances payment, let him advance it for known dates, known weight, known measure, to a known term."
"523","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated from Ibn Abi Husayn and Fitr that they heard Abu al-Tufayl say: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened around the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah and that it is a sunnah. Ibn Abbas said: They spoke truth and falsehood. Fitr meant: they spoke truth — he did hasten — and they spoke falsely — it is not a sunnah."
"524","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: I came to Ibn Abbas at Arafah and found him eating pomegranate. He said: Come near and eat; perhaps you are fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not fast this day."
"525","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Hunayn, the freedman of the family of al-Abbas, informed me, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Abbas marvel at one who fasts ahead of the month, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see it, fast; and when you see it, break fast; and if it is obscured for you, complete the count as thirty."
"526","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah narrating from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Madinah in the year of the Conquest in the month of Ramadan, fasting until when he reached al-Kadid he broke fast. He said: And only the latter of the action of the Messenger of Allah is taken. Sufyan said: I do not know whether al-Zuhri said it from Ubaydullah or from Ibn Abbas."
"527","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Jubayr informed me, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah while the Jews were fasting the day of Ashura. He said: What is this day that you fast? He said: This is a great day; Allah saved Musa in it and drowned the family of Pharaoh in it, so Musa fasted it in gratitude. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are more entitled to Musa than you. So he fasted it and ordered its fast."
"528","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you, when he comes to his wife, says: In the name of Allah; O Allah, keep Satan from us and keep Satan from what You grant us — then if a child is decreed between them, Satan shall never harm him."
"529","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The previously married woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin is consulted about herself; her silence is her consent."
"530","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a man, when he conducted li'an between the two invoking curses, to place his hand upon his mouth at the fifth. And Sufyan would sometimes say in it: For it is decisive."
"531","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say: Ibn Abbas mentioned the two invoking curses, and Abdullah ibn Shaddad said to him: Is it she about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I stoned anyone without proof, I would have stoned her? Ibn Abbas said: No; that is a woman who did openly."
"532","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your garments are the white; let your living wear them, and shroud your dead in them. And the best of your kohls is ithmid, for it clears the sight and grows the hair."
"533","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: If people reduced in bequests to a quarter, it would be dearer to me, due to the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A third — and a third is much."
"534","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that Sa'd ibn Ubadah sought a ruling from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a vow upon his mother, who died before fulfilling it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Fulfill it on her behalf."
"535","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abbas, that a man died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving no heir but a slave he had freed, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him his inheritance."
"536","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away leaving nine, and he used to apportion to eight."
"537","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd al-Karim al-Jazari say: I heard Ikrimah say: I heard Ibn Abbas narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade blowing into the vessel or breathing into it."
"538","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abi Muslim al-Ahwal — and he was trustworthy — narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Thursday — and what is Thursday? Then he wept until his tears wet the pebbles. It was said to him: O Abu Abbas, what is Thursday? He said: The pain of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intensified on Thursday, and he said: Bring me; I shall write for you a writing after which you shall never go astray. They disputed, and disputing is not fitting in the presence of a prophet. He said: What is wrong with him? Has he become delirious? Ask him for clarity. They repeated it to him, and he said: Leave me; what I am in is better than what you call me to. He said: And he enjoined three upon them, saying: Expel the polytheists from the Arabian Peninsula; honor the delegations with the like of what I used to honor them with. Sufyan said: Sulayman said: I do not know whether Sa'id mentioned the third and I forgot it, or he was silent about it."
"539","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Abi A'ishah — and he was among the trustworthy — narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Qur'an was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would move his tongue with it wanting to memorize it. So Allah revealed: Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it. Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation."
"540","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr — and he did not mention Ibn Abbas in it — who said: When the Qur'an was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would hasten with it wanting to memorize it. So Allah revealed: Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it. Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not know the end of a surah until there was revealed to him: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate."
"541","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us — and I heard him mention a scene he witnessed, then he would breathe and weep, in it so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so and Miqsam. Sa'id ibn Jubayr said: Did all of you hear what is said about food? Miqsam said: Narrate to the people, O Abu Abdullah. Sa'id ibn Jubayr said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing descends in the middle of the food, so eat from its sides and do not eat from its middle."
"542","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, saying: I heard Ikrimah say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have no evil example: the one who takes back his gift is like the dog returning to its vomit."
"543","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes an image shall be punished and burdened to breathe spirit into it, yet he cannot; and whoever falsely claims a dream shall be punished and burdened to tie between two grains of barley, yet he cannot tie; and whoever listens to the talk of a people averse to him shall have molten lead poured into his ear on the Day of Resurrection. Sufyan said: Al-anuk is lead."
"544","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz, who said: Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about the woman and the slave who attend the conquest — is a share allotted to them; about killing children; about the orphan — when does the name of orphanhood cease for him; and about the near kin — who are they? He said: Write, O Yazid; were it not that he would fall into folly, I would not write to him. Write: You wrote to me asking me about the near kin — who are they; and we used to claim that we are they, but our people refused it to us. You wrote asking me about the woman and the slave who attend the conquest — is anything allotted to them; and nothing is allotted to them, but they are given something. You wrote asking me about the orphan — when does the name of orphanhood cease for him; and the name of orphanhood does not cease for him until he reaches maturity and sound judgment is perceived in him. You wrote asking me about killing children; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not kill them, and you shall not kill them unless you know of them what the companion of Musa knew of the boy he killed."
"545","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from Ikrimah, who said: When it reached Ibn Abbas that Ali burned the apostates — meaning the heretics — Ibn Abbas said: Had I been there, I would have killed them, due to the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever changes his religion, kill him. And I would not have burned them, due to the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): It befits no one to punish with the punishment of Allah. Sufyan said: Ammar al-Duhni, while in the gathering — the gathering of Amr ibn Dinar — with Ayyub narrating this hadith, said: Ali did not burn them; rather he dug tunnels for them and smoked them from them until he killed them. Amr ibn Dinar said: Did you not hear their speaker as he says:"
"546","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu al-Juwayriyah al-Jarmi say: I asked Ibn Abbas, while he was leaning his back upon the Ka'bah, about al-badhaq — and I, by Allah, was the first of the Arabs to ask him — and he said: Muhammad preceded al-badhaq; and whatever intoxicates is forbidden."
"547","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Abi Ya'qub — and he was of my age or younger than me — narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Jibril: Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill? He said: The fuller and more complete of them."
"548","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ubaydullah — then in the last period of Sufyan he affirmed Ibn Abbas in it — who said: There came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), upon his return from Uhud, a man who said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw a cloud dripping clarified butter and honey, and I saw people scooping from it — some taking much of it and some little; and I saw a rope reaching to the sky: you took hold of it, and Allah raised you; then a man after you took hold of it and rose; then another after him and rose; then another after him, and it was cut with him; then it was joined for him and he rose. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, let me interpret it. He said: Interpret it. He said: As for the cloud, it is Islam; and as for its dripping clarified butter and honey, with people scooping from it, it is the Qur'an — its sweetness and its softness — some taking much of it and some little; and as for the rope reaching to the sky, it is what you are upon of the truth: you took hold of it and Allah raised you; then a man after you shall take hold of it and rise by it; then another after him and rise; then another after him, and it shall be cut with him; then it shall be joined for him and he shall rise. O Messenger of Allah, did I get it right? He said: You got part right and erred in part. He said: I adjure you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not adjure, O Abu Bakr."
"549","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, saying: My father informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Ja'far say: When the news of the death of Ja'far ibn Abi Talib came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them what occupies them."
"550","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: My father informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Ja'far say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me, me and a boy of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, and carried us upon a beast, so we were three."
"551","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, saying: A man of Fahm informed me, saying: We were with Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr at Muzdalifah when he slaughtered a camel for us. Abdullah ibn Ja'far said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be served meat. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of meat is the meat of the back."
"552","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to us, saying: My father informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Ja'far say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating fresh dates with cucumber."
"553","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Husayn informed me, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan, from Usamah ibn Zayd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever, nor the disbeliever from the Muslim."
"554","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Usamah ibn Zayd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked out over a fortress of the fortresses of Madinah and said: Do you see what I see? I see tribulations falling among your houses like the falling of rain."
"555","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us — countless times beyond counting — saying: My father informed me, saying: Usamah ibn Zayd was asked — and I was beside him, and he had been riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafah until he came to Muzdalifah — how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travel when he moved on? He said: He traveled at a gentle pace; when he found an open space, he hastened. Sufyan said: Hisham said: And al-nass is above al-anaq."
"556","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas saying: A man came to Sa'd asking him about the plague, while Usama ibn Zayd was with him, so Usama said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is a punishment or a scourge sent upon some people among those before you, or upon a party of the Children of Israel; it comes at times and goes at times; so if it breaks out in a land while you are in it, do not leave it fleeing from it, and if you hear of it in a land, do not enter it. So Amr said: Perhaps for some people it is a punishment or scourge, and for some people it is martyrdom. Sufyan said: This statement of Amr pleased me."
"557","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid narrated to me, saying: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: Usama ibn Zayd informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Usury is in deferment. Abu Bakr said: Sufyan would sometimes not raise it as a Prophetic report, and he was questioned about that, so he said: I hold back from it at times out of dislike of money-exchange disputes; but as raised, it is raised."
"558","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Marwan ibn Muawiya narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Usama ibn Zayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not left behind me for my community a trial more harmful to men than women."
"559","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-A'mash narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Wa'il saying: It was said to Usama ibn Zayd: Will you not speak to Uthman? He said: Do you think I do not speak to him except by letting you hear; I speak to him privately without opening a door of which I would be the first to open it. Then he said: Indeed I will not say of a man who was set over me as a ruler that he is the best of people, after something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man who was a ruler will be brought and cast into the Fire, and his intestines will spill out, and he will go round in the Fire as the donkey goes round with the millstone; then the people of the Fire will gather to him and say: Were you not commanding us to right and forbidding us from wrong? He will say: I used to command you to right and not do it, and forbid you from wrong and do it."
"560","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Uqba and Muhammad ibn Abi Harmala narrated to us — Sufyan said: one of them said: Kurayb informed me, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama, and the other said: Kurayb informed me, from Usama — and he was the riding companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafat until he reached Muzdalifa — he said: I set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Arafat, and when he reached the mountain pass he dismounted and urinated, and he did not say: he poured out water; then I brought him the small waterskin and he performed a light ablution, so I said: The prayer, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The prayer is ahead of you. Then when he reached Muzdalifa he prayed Maghrib, then they untied their saddles, then he prayed Isha. Sufyan said: Ibrahim ibn Uqba and Muhammad did not differ in anything of this hadith except that one said: Kurayb, from Usama, and the other said: Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Usama."
"561","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us that he heard Sulayman ibn Yasar narrating from Abu Rafi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not command me to camp there, meaning at al-Abtah, but I myself pitched his tent, then he came and stayed there. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, and Amr ibn Dinar used to narrate this hadith from Salih ibn Kaysan, so when Salih came to us, Amr said to us: Go to him and ask him about this hadith."
"562","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Salim Abu al-Nadr, freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Ma'mar, narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father. Sufyan said: And Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us in disconnected form, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let me not find one of you reclining on his couch when there comes to him a matter of my affair, of what I commanded or forbade, and he says: I do not know; whatever we found in the Book of Allah, we followed it. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: I remember the hadith of Ibn al-Munkadir better, because I heard it first, though I have also memorized this one."
"563","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Maysara narrated to us, saying: I heard Amr ibn al-Sharid saying: Al-Miswar ibn Makhrama took my hand and said: Let us go to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. So I went out with him, with his hand upon one of my shoulders, and Abu Rafi came to him and said to al-Miswar: Will you not tell this one, meaning Sa'd, to buy my two rooms in his house. Sa'd said: By Allah, I will not add more than four hundred dinars, either in installments or deferred payments. Abu Rafi said to him: By Allah, I used to withhold it from five hundred dinars in cash, and were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The neighbor has more right to his adjoining property, I would not sell to you."
"564","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib informed me that they heard Hakim ibn Hizam saying: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then he said: This wealth is fresh and sweet; whoever takes it with a generous heart, it is blessed for him in it, and whoever takes it with an aspiring heart, it is not blessed for him in it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied; and the upper hand is better than the lower hand. Sufyan said: I heard nothing but this."
"565","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, that he heard Hakim ibn Hizam saying: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I freed forty slaves in the pre-Islamic age. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: You embraced Islam with the good you had done before."
"566","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have names: I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and I am al-Mahi by whom disbelief is effaced, and I am al-Hashir at whose heels people will be gathered, and I am al-Aqib, and al-Aqib is the one after whom there is no prophet."
"567","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri narrating from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib the chapter of al-Tur. Sufyan said: They said concerning this hadith that Jubayr said: I heard it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was a polytheist, and my heart almost flew; but al-Zuhri did not say it to us."
"568","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri narrating, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No severer of ties will enter Paradise. Sufyan said: Its explanation is: the severer of kinship."
"569","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, and I heard him narrating it, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, if Allah wills, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had Mut'im ibn Adi been alive and then spoken to me concerning these foul ones, or concerning these captives, I would have released them for him — meaning the captives of Badr. And when Sufyan narrated this hadith and mentioned the report in it, he would say: if Allah wills, without omitting it; and if he did not mention the report in it, he would sometimes say: if Allah wills, and sometimes not say it."
"570","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me, from his father, who said: I lost a camel of mine on the day of Arafat, so I went out seeking it at Arafat and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing with the people at Arafat, so I said: He is of the Hums; what is he doing here? Sufyan said: Al-Ahmas is the one strict in his religion, and Quraysh were called the Hums; and Satan had lured them and said to them: If you venerate other than your sanctuary, people will hold your sanctuary lightly, so they would not go out of the Sanctuary."
"571","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Qays al-A'raj — brother of Umar ibn Qays, freedman of Banu Fazara — narrated to us, from Mujahid, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand at Arafat in all his years."
"572","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Abdullah ibn Babah narrating, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd al-Muttalib — or: O sons of Abd Manaf — if you are put in charge of anything of this affair, do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House and prays at whatever hour he wishes, of night or day."
"573","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Abu Najih informed me, from Khalid ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah seized a man of the land for something, and Khalid ibn al-Walid spoke to him about it, and it was said to him: You have angered the commander. Khalid said: I did not intend to anger him, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The severest of people in punishment with Allah on the Day of Resurrection are the severest of them in punishing people in this world."
"574","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to take Aisha behind him on the mount and perform her Umra from al-Tan'im. Sufyan said: And this is the chapter of Shu'ba — he informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him — meaning: connected."
"575","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: My father gave me a wedding feast during the rule of Uthman and invited people to our banquet, and among those who came to us was Safwan ibn Umayya, who said: Tear the meat with your teeth, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is more wholesome and more agreeable — or: more wholesome and more healing."
"576","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hajabi narrated to us, saying: My maternal uncle Musafi ibn Shayba informed me, from my mother Safiyya bint Shayba, who said: A woman of Banu Sulaym who delivered most of the people of their household informed me that she asked Uthman ibn Talha about the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him after his entering the Kaaba, so he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: If you saw the ram's horns in the House and I forgot to order you to cover them, then cover them; for there should not be in the House anything that distracts the worshipper."
"577","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Musawir al-Warraq narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Hurayth al-Makhzumi informed me, from his father, who said: I saw upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a black turban on the day of the conquest of Mecca."
"578","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Sari, from Amr ibn Hurayth, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in the dawn prayer: By the night when it covers."
"579","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Abdullah ibn Muti informed me, from his father Muti ibn al-Aswad — and he was of the disobedient ones of Quraysh who were named al-As, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Muti, and none of the disobedient ones of Quraysh attained Islam but him — saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Mecca saying: No Qurashi shall be killed as a bound prisoner after this day ever. Sufyan said: Meaning upon disbelief."
"580","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Zam'a ibn al-Aswad saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he mentioned the one who hamstrung the she-camel — saying: A man of might and power among his people volunteered for it, like Abu Zam'a. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned women and said: One of you deliberately goes to his wife and beats her as he beats a slave, then embraces her at the end of the day. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reproached them for laughing at flatulence, saying: Why does one of you laugh at what he himself does?"
"581","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated to us that he heard Abu Nu'aym Wahb ibn Kaysan saying: I heard Umar ibn Abi Salama saying: I was an orphan boy in the care of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my hand would roam about the dish, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O boy, when you eat, mention the name of Allah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is near you. He said: That remained my manner of eating after that."
"582","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Umar ibn Abi Salama, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in the house of Umm Salama in a single garment wrapped about him."
"583","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith ibn Malik ibn al-Barsa, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Mecca saying: Mecca shall never be raided after this day ever. Sufyan said: Its explanation is: upon disbelief."
"584","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Umayya narrated to us, from Ibn al-Khuwar, freedman of Banu Amir, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard al-Harith ibn Malik ibn al-Barsa during the pilgrimage season calling out among the people — Sufyan said: I do not know it but that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one who swears a false oath to cut off thereby the right of a Muslim man but that he will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"585","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, saying: I heard Kurz ibn Alqama al-Khuza'i saying: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, does Islam have an end? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes; whatever household among the Arabs or non-Arabs Allah intends good for, He brings Islam into it. He said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then trials will fall like dark clouds. The man said to him: Nay, by Allah, if Allah wills, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, they will return therein as coiled black snakes, some striking the necks of others. Al-Zuhri said: Al-Aswad is the snake when it wants to bite; it rises up thus — and al-Humaydi raised his hand — then it strikes down. Sufyan said when he narrated this hadith: You need not care if you do not hear this from Ibn Shihab."
"586","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed me, from Abu Shurayh al-Ka'bi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him do good to his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest."
"587","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Shurayh, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it, adding: Hospitality is three days, and whatever exceeds is charity; and his due gift is a day and a night; and it is not lawful for him to stay with him until he causes him hardship."
"588","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Safwan al-Jumahi informed me that he heard a man of his maternal uncles of Azd called Yazid ibn Shayban saying: Ibn Mirba' al-Ansari came to us while we were at Arafat in a place which Amr kept distant from the standing place of the imam, and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to you, saying: Remain upon these rites of yours, for you are upon an inheritance from the inheritance of Ibrahim, peace be upon him. Abu Bakr said: And Sufyan would sometimes say: Stand firm, and sometimes say: Your father Ibrahim."
"589","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib narrated to me, from one of his family, that he heard his grandfather al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'a saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying toward the door of Banu Sahm while people passed in front of him, with no screen between him and the circumambulation."
"590","Sufyan said: And Ibn Jurayj first narrated to us, from Kathir, from his father, from al-Muttalib; then when I asked him about it he said: It is not from my father; rather one of my family informed me that he heard it from al-Muttalib."
"591","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ismail ibn Umayya narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, that he heard Uqba ibn al-Harith saying: I married the daughter of Abu Ihab, then a black woman came and said: I suckled you both. So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his right and asked him, and he turned away from me; then I went to him from his left and he turned away from me; then I faced him and asked him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, though she is black, though she... though she... So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How, when it has been said?"
"592","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to us, saying: I heard Isa ibn Talha ibn Ubaydullah narrating, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, I slaughtered before stoning. He said: Stone, and there is no harm. And another said: I shaved before slaughtering? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Slaughter, and there is no harm. It was said to Sufyan: Is this of what you memorized from al-Zuhri? He said: Yes, as if hearing it, except that it is long and I memorized this of it; then Bulbul — also called Bulayl, son of Harb — said to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrates from you that you said: I did not memorize it? He said: He spoke truly; I did not memorize all of it, but this I mastered."
"593","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to us, saying: My father informed me, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, mighty and exalted, does not take away knowledge by snatching it from the hearts of men, but takes it by taking the scholars; then when He leaves no scholar, people take ignorant heads and ask them, and they give verdicts without knowledge, so they go astray and lead astray. Urwa said: Then I stayed a year, then I met Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As in circumambulation and asked him about it, and he informed me of it."
"594","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Iyad, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vessels, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, not all people find a waterskin. So he permitted them earthen jars that were not coated with pitch."
"595","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, saying: My father informed me: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two traits, easy, yet few act upon them, and no Muslim guards them but enters Paradise. They said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: You glorify Allah after every prayer ten times, magnify ten times, and praise ten times; and you glorify at your sleep thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times. Then Sufyan said: One of them is thirty-four. That is two hundred and fifty upon the tongue, and two thousand five hundred upon the scale. Abdullah ibn Amr said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counting them on his hand; then he said: Which of you does in his day and night two thousand five hundred evil deeds? They said: O Messenger of Allah, how can they not be guarded? He said: Satan comes to one of you and says to him: Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such, until he gets up without saying them. Sufyan said: This is the first thing we asked Ata about; and Ayyub ordered people, when Ata came to Basra, to go to him and ask him about this hadith. [flag: source brackets a repeated sub-clause (scribal duplication); rendered once]"
"596","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to pledge to you upon emigration, leaving my parents weeping. He said: Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep."
"597","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas al-Sa'ib ibn Farrukh, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it, except that he said: Then in them both strive in struggle."
"598","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amir informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not show mercy to our young and recognize the right of our elder."
"599","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Suhayb, freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir, informed me, saying: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills a sparrow or anything above it without its right, Allah, mighty and exalted, will question him about its killing. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is its right? He said: He slaughters it and eats it, and does not cut off its head and throw it away. It was said to Sufyan: Hammad ibn Zayd says in it: Amr informed me, from Suhayb al-Hadhdha? Sufyan said: I never heard Amr say Suhayb al-Hadhdha at all; he said nothing but Suhayb, freedman of Abdullah ibn Amir."
"600","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Aws al-Thaqafi informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Amr saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The just upon the Day of Resurrection with Allah are upon pulpits of light at the right of the Most Merciful — and both His hands are right — those who are just in their judgment and their families and what they were put in charge of."
